{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us","id":999231,"title":"The Vigil in the US","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-06T08:39:48-08:00","id":999231,"title":"The Vigil in the US","content":"So I've been wondering about how to describe the Vigil in the cities other gamelines use, canon and fan. These are my best takes, but if anyone has any additional information they know would help expand on this or correct anything I got wrong, feel free to tell me so I can edit it in. First, New Orleans.<br /> <br /> <b>New Orleans: Blood by the Bayous</b><br /> <br /> New Orleans has always been a hunter madhouse, but unlike the near-open warfare in Philadelphia New Orleans is a backstabbing, Machiavellian situation where hunters must wrangle with an entrenched vampire power structure that's probably existed as long as the city has. The leeches run the entire area, their fangs stretching at least as far as East Baton Rouge in terms of control. Hunters have always been inside the city, but aside from the conspiracies local cells and less established compacts have always been quickly destroyed by the vampires before they could really do anything. Since the 80s, however, the hunters are able to more easily organize across long distances and occult information is more easily available. Now the city's hunters are rumored to be planning a major offensive against the leeches, something not seen since Philly's Fairmount Reclamation in the 70s. Unlike Fairmount, any effort to try and clean New Orleans will result in a long, grueling battle that everyone knows can't be won in a single night.<br /> <br /> <b>Ahl al-Jabal:</b><b> Screened</b><b>:</b> Though Islam isn't a populous faith in Louisiana, a large cell in the Louisiana State Penitentiary at Angola has managed to keep tabs on the entire state for the compact relatively effectively. In New Orleans, the compact takes great care to never associate with the local mosques or community hubs, knowing that the vampires could very easily turn Islamophobia to a weapon against the innocents. Instead, the compact has wormed its way into the criminal underworld, using the criminals to cover their actions against mid-level vampires and their slaves.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru: Seeking:</b> Faced with a well-established presence of local witches, shapeshifters, and vampires, the Aegis operated in New Orleans with a light touch. Individual cells tend to focus their efforts at locating and acquiring any relics as discretely and quickly as possible. While the years that followed Hurricane Katrina allowed them to secure a few notable items of power, the conspiracy remains a small group in the city.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones: Syncretized:</b> Like the Ahl al-Jabal, the Cult of the Phoenix does not identify too strongly with Islam to avoid painting a target on for the vampires. Their cell in New Orleans was greatly influenced by the local culture, though, to the point that elements of Voodoo were woven into their predominantly Christian practices. Louisiana's Ascending Ones thus tend to use their Elixirs to imbue an assortment of artifacts and charms rather than directly imbibing them.<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey: Mardi Gras:</b> As far as the Abbey is concerned, every day in New Orleans in a funeral parade. Often they'll parade through the streets with a staked vampire in a casket, twirling umbrellas as a brass band plays on. The vampires don't seem to mind however, often joining for the macabre revelry so they can join in with the Abbey for the inevitable afterparty.<br /> <br /> <b>Barrett Commission: Entrenched:</b> The Commission has always watched Louisiana, and New Orleans especially, with nervousness since they first made it to the city in 1866 post-war. Able to easily maneuver through the entrenched corruption inherent in the city's power structure, the Commission has steadily been fortifying itself by using other hunters as the cat's paws to test the strength of the vampires through the years. Focusing on making sure the corrupt in the city are <i>their</i> corrupt, the Commission is rumored to have made a long list of names that they plan on using to finally get a leg up when the time is right.<br /> <br /> <b>The Cainite Heresey: Rampant:</b> Cainites are practically everywhere in New Orleans, a constant plague that refuses to die off. Typically the other hunter groups just let the Cainites do as they will so long as they stay away from their turf, but lately the Cainites are getting more riled up than usual, and that's saying something. Due to their secretive nature, no one knows what has the cult so riled, but several cells have mentioned that maybe the time has come to finally muzzle the mad dog.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron Group: Stable:</b> Cheiron's subsidiary in New Orleans, Delta Medical Systems Inc, doesn't have as bad of a time in the city as their sister company in Philadelphia with finding new subjects/goods. Local unemployed are more than willing to take on any job they can, and the constant stream of vampires in the city means that they have a solid resource to draw on for a steady income.<br /> <br /> <b>Les Mysteres: Faceted: </b>Les Mysteres have basically been in New Orleans since the 1700s, a part of the city's culture that no vampire could wipe out. Though the group as a whole is more well-known for focusing on werewolves, the <i>mambo</i> and <i>houngan </i>of the group have faced more vampires than they can care to remember. In particular, they have become well known for their opposition against a group of vampires claiming to use their magics to call on the spirits, something their friends tell the cells is a blasphemy.<br /> <br /> <b>The Long Night:</b> <b>Humbled:</b> The intense vampiric presence in the city effectively destroyed the first time the Long Night tried to move in on New Orleans, killing the cell and ghouling the cell's pastor. Since then the Long Night has had to face the fact that faith isn't enough to break the vampire hold in the city. Instead, they've focused on the forgotten and cast out of the city, believing that they can at least deny the vampires an easy source of food. The Hopeless and Merciful of the compact run things, making the Long Night a support rather than a frontline ally.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule: Brokering:</b> The heavy French presence in New Orleans made it hard for the members of the Loyalists setting up after WWII to move inconspicuously. Thankfully they found several groups of occultists in the city willing to speak with them and, if necessary, work with them. Though not ancient, as a port city New Orleans traffics in every conceivable industry and all kinds of goods. The Loyalists have used this to their advantage, acting as information brokers between the various hunter cells in exchange for information on anything they might take an interest in. If not, it's cold hard cash.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge: Subtle:</b> The presence of the vampires controlling so many old-blooded families in New Orleans has forced the Lucifuge to accept that they have to hold back on the hellfire and demonic familiars. Instead, the Lucifiuge cell in the city prefers to focus on the high-class ghouled that the vampires claim to gain access to more money and power. Several families have actually been freed from the vampires, but one family remains fully entrenched and almost willing to accept their state of affairs; the Crassus.<br /> <br /> <b>Maiden's Blood Sisterhood: Weathered:</b> With cells in Tulane and U of Louisiana, the Sisterhood have been forced to acknowledge that the vampires run everything, and the universities are considered prime feeding grounds. Though normally the cells of the Sisterhood would maybe face an elder vampire if they were truly unlucky, in New Orleans elder vampires seem to be everywhere you can swing a stake. Casualties have been high, and the vampires have used everything from campus administration to controlling frats and student organizations to wipe out their enemies. This has only made the Sisterhood even more resolute in their goals to protect their campuses.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum: Firm:</b> The strong Catholic city has fed the local Malleus cells for decades, with their strongest presence protecting the students at Loyala University. Though vampires have continually tried to break the Malleus by use of their heretical belief that vampire's are somehow God's chosen demons, the Mother Church continues to press back against this by continually purging local parishes and the dioceses of any malicious influence.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero: Broken:</b> In an astounding reality for many to face, Network Zero has been forced to hold back on trying to expose the vampires in the city. Casualties just kept piling up so fast that the cells in the city had to coalesce into one to keep from being wiped out, even running to the Night Watch for protection. Now the cell is forced to remain the hunter information network for what everyone knows, rather than the secret information the Loyalists specialize in.<br /> <br /> <b>Night Watch: On the Front:</b> Outside of Pittsburgh, the Night Watch has their strongest presence in New Orleans. Former ghouls, attack survivors, volunteers who found the truth, the Night Watch in New Orleans is still led by the last surviving original leader of the Watch, Andre Sandoval. Though bound to his wheelchair, Sandoval's presence has continued to inspire the Watch in the city to keep fighting. Both vampires and street gangs have reason to fear the Watch, as their volunteer patrols in the streets combined with their continued presence in the shadows have actually managed to become a thorn in many a vampire's side in the city they control. Many can safely claim that the Night Watch are the driving force behind the rumored campaign against the vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis:</b> <b>Studying:</b> Null Mysteriis isn't a large presence in the city, but there are two cells in the city; one at Tulane, one at the new University Medical Center New Orleans. Both primarily made up of medical experts, the cells are unfortunately working at cross purposes. The cell at Tulane are trying to figure out how to block people from being ghouled, the cell at UMCNO trying to find a way to figure out the method by which ghouls don't age. Both have made headway, but the real worry is a disease that broke out just before Katrina hit, treatable but dangerous to anyone who contracts it. Both cells want to research it, but fear that improper containment will lead to an outbreak.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE:</b><b> Patrolling:</b> With the headquarters of the USMC reserve in New Orleans, coupled with efforts by the world's leading asshole DA Jim Garrison, TFV has been a presence in the city since the 1980s. Though at times willing to get their hands dirty in the streets, many hunters have noted that the MIBs are just as content to go around intimidating other hunters to back off from certain leeches they claim, &quot;Aren't worth the wood for the stake&quot;. Of course, this is after a massive sweep through the city during Katrina where dozens of TWILIGHT MRUs essentially cleansed the city of any vampire that wasn't smart enough to go into hiding during the storm.<br /> <br /> <b>The Union: Underground:</b> After the last state governor, the Union had to face harsh anti-labor opposition that the vampires seized on with gusto. Facing reality, the Union in the city backed off to let the night watch handle the bulk of the vampire problem. Now, however, the Union wants to start pressing forward again. Unfortunately, many hunters consider the Union a relic of a bygone era, and recruiting new members has been difficult with the more known actions of the Night Watch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 11-21-2016, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T18:11:05-08:00","id":999510,"title":"","content":"<b>Denver: Wild in the Rockies</b><br /> <br /> The greater Denver area has been a werewolf hunting ground for years, and for the past two decades hunters have tried to burn out the packs from the surrounding county without success. What is known is that there's some kind of ongoing werewolf war between two factions, and that one faction just hates hunters while the other wants them for breakfast, lunch, and dinner. Specialists against werewolves have been trying to figure out exactly why the wolves are so intent on flocking to Denver in such numbers, and why they are apparently dead-set on purging the city of both their enemies and hunters alike. Some hunters have begun to think that it might have something to do with the legendary Rocky Mountains themselves, that some great occult power resides inside them as both a symbol and a physical location.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru: Possessed:</b> The AKD in the US see Denver as a bit of a grail. On the one hand, clearing it out would create untold misery for the conspiracy and their allies. But if they could finally defeat the shapeshifters in what is seen as their stronghold, it would mean that the Shield and Spear can claim a real, true victory against their ancient enemies. This has led the conspiracy to a take-no-prisoners system, one that continually hamstrings hunters who are trying to find out what, exactly, is going on.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Barrett Commission: Cat and Mouse: </b>Unlike most cities in the US, Denver's politicians are under the control of the werewolves rather than vampires. This has made Denver a dangerous region for the Commission to operate in, as nearly all the vampires in the city seem to live in fear of the werewolves who treat anyone who knows that they exist as a deathly threat rather than an inconvenience. This has the commission cell in Denver wondering if maybe it can't use the werewolves as a tool once they take back city hall.<br /> <br /> <b>Bear Lodge: Growing:</b> As others plot to retake the Montana Lodge, the Denver Lodge sees new members practically every other week with how often hunters report their stumbling into sacred werewolf sites.Though not driven by anything more than their desire to be the best hunters on Earth, a growing trend in the Denver lodge has been to dress up their actions as trying to cull a rampant species of predator that has been left unchecked for too long.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron Group:</b> <b>Opportunistic:</b> Rasend Pharmaceutical LLC doesn't want to risk its own people or security on traipsing through the wilderness seeking werewolves it knows would happily gut an office building full of innocent people just for being the place one single hunter worked during the day. So Rasend Pharma has decided to put out generous bounties for dead werewolves (it's already figured out ways to keep slashers from profiting off their sicknesses), and incredible prizes for live ones.<br /> <br /> <b>Illuminated Brotherhood: Warning: </b>The Brotherhood isn't very active in Denver, what with high casualties and few willing to actually brave such strange company. Their only real cell is in the University of Denver, but with the right pharmacology the group can explore the entire Denver region. What they've told is that there are mighty spirits roaming the outskirts of the city, things that look like warped pictures out of a natural history book, though no other hunters take these stories seriously.<br /> <br /> <b>Keepers of the Source: Present:</b> About all that can be said about the Keepers is that they have a cell or two in the Denver area. Active in regional conservation movements, the Keepers have reportedly made contact with a werewolf pack that might be willing to sit down and talk with the hunters to try and at least tell the hunters who the bad werewolves are. Most other hunters in the area brush such claims off as a trap in the making with bait that doesn't even realize what could happen.<br /> <br /> <b>Les Mysteries: Quiet:</b> Taking their cues from what they claim is Native American spiritualism (In reality just a synchronized belief system of facts about tribal beliefs, Hollywood crap, and how people <i>think</i> is Native American spiritualism), Les Mysteries in Denver know that the werewolves would come down on them hard if they made themselves loud like the Bear Lodge. Instead, the &quot;shamans&quot; of Les Mysteries are doing their best to lay low and observe their foes. They've also seen the strange spirit-things wandering outside Denver, but their &quot;spirit guides&quot; tell them that these are at best just a small problem compared to the wolves.<br /> <br /> <b>Long Night: Welcoming:</b> Certain werewolves have expressed that they can't stand what they've become, and believe that religion can save them. The churches of the Long Night are more than willing to offer salvation to these lost souls, though most hunters don't see that in the Long Night surrounding Denver. They see compounds meant to exclude the outside world, cult-like practices thick with groupthink and love bombings. While many hunters fear the Long Night in Kansas, some fear that Denver and the werewolves will spark the next Waco.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule: Hiking:</b> The Loyalists aren't interested in Denver, nor the fighting between the hunters or werewolves. The Loyalists have been sighted out in the less populated areas of Denver and the countryside to look for ancient sites left behind by the Uta people that once lived in the Denver area. This has caused some trouble however, as descendants of the Ute that still remain in the area claim the Loyalists are robbing their ancestral sites for their own selfish ends. Deafening silence from the Loyalists hasn't helped matters.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge: Lean:</b> There are at best maybe three members of the Lucifuge in all of Colorado, all situated in the state capitol. This has forced them to rely on patsies and &quot;followers&quot;, but also to remain relatively insulted from their vicious opponents. Using their support to weaken the werewolves, the trio arrange to confront these weakened beasts to decide whether they're to be allowed to rebuild and remain undisturbed, or to burn the werewolf before it can cause more trouble.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum: Shepherding:</b> The Malleus in Denver have their churches protected against the werewolves, true. But the Inquisition is more concerned about the spiritual battle raging in the city. Caring less about what's legalized, the Malleus exorcists are busy rushing from brushfire to brushfire trying to save the city from full-scale possessions and outbreaks of demonic activity. Thankfully the influx of immigrants from Central America gives the city a strong base of support to draw on regardless of what the wolves might try.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero: Scouting:</b> With nightly werewolf battles, Network Zero trail cameras are out in full force. Several of the videos have already gone viral, but this has drawn attention from both the more tech-savvy wolves and the conspiracies. Staying relatively low since the release of said videos, Network Zero has had to face the fact that the werewolves can use technology just as well as any man and are beginning to track down cell members when the videos are released.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis: Exploring:</b> Like Network Zero, Null Mysteriis has become a stable fixture in the area outside of Denver. The difference is the bulk of Mysteriis members are biologists and anthropologists, studying the werewolves for signs of how their culture works and how their bodies function both in the &quot;wild&quot; and in the urban environments. This has actually placed ORAS cells the closest to cracking the differences between the two werewolf factions, but they won't release any findings until they have a more concrete understanding. The cells in the Denver area understand that if they release bad information, people <i>will</i> die.<br /> <br /> <b>Talbot Group: Frayed:</b> Coming to accept that no, werewolves <i>aren't</i> meant to be solely human, the Talbot Group's Denver affiliates are instead focusing on the werewolf victims. They've also noticed a large amount of spiritual. activity and possessions under their aegis as well. Slowly trying to work out with the formerly possessed patients in their care how they think it happened, the victims have only vague recollections that whatever took them over was under the impression that it could do whatever it wanted because no one could stop them.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE: Sequestered:</b> The closest TFV presence to Denver is in Cheyenne Mountain (Jokingly called SGC), so the MIBs don't often run into trouble in the city. The problem is when the werewolves keep trying to get onto the base itself. Several times TFV operatives have been forced to neutralize werewolves trespassing on the mountain, but none have ever been willing to state why. The mountain was checked six ways to Sunday before the complex was built, so as far as TFV is concerned there shouldn't be a reason for the infiltration in the first place.<br /> <br /> <b>The Union: Defensive:</b> Like werewolves, the Union is oriented on the territory it protects. Union neighborhoods in Denver are practically considered no-go zones by all werewolves in Denver and the surrounding area, but by process of looking into the abyss Union neighborhoods are just as dangerous to outsiders as well. Hunters expecting a relatively wary group of hunters based of their experiences in other cities are in for a shock when the Union confronts them violently for stepping on their turf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 11-10-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T04:18:31-08:00","id":999662,"title":"","content":"I'm working on a Princess city book for Detroit with Super_Dave and it includes a lot of hunters (you've got to have allies to interact with socally after all).<br /> <br /> Have a look if you're interested: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17vKlzHddpi-5PVLHy8yuonVH3rqbrawiNLDz35gBlGc/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...?pref=2&amp;pli=1#</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T10:09:29-08:00","id":1000311,"title":"","content":"<b>Boston: Mad Magic Mayhem</b><br /> <br /> Boston has become a city with a reputation for trouble in the hunter community, as hunters and witches battle practically every single night to try and force each other to a stalemate. From the colleges to the dockyards to the suburbs, Boston is a massive chess game of backstabbing, ambushes, and politicking between multiple groups of wizards that claim the city as theirs. Worse, the city is filled with as many if not more occult secrets as Philadelphia, leftovers from the founding of the nation itself that could hold powerful occult objects and secrets for whoever uncovers the truth.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru: Driven: </b>As one of the largest cities with a confirmed large population of witches in the population in North America, the AKD continually devote large resources to the city in the hopes that they can continue to seize the relics and artifacts left in the wake of conflict with them. ALready several major relics have been found and catalogued, as well as several prisoners taken in the hopes that more can be located soon. Why soon? No one needs to know apparently.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones: Angry:</b> The Cult of the Phoenix in Boston used to have a near-monopoly on the drug trade in the city through various patsies and contacts, but in the past decade someone has decided to take a cut of the action. Someone's selling a new drug on the market, one that not only gives a killer high but has a kind of magical trace to it as well. This competition in terms of business and product is threatening the Ascending Ones, and they don't like to be threatened.<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey: Comfortable:</b> Home to many of the nation's most powerful, established, and wealthy families, Boston and the Abbey go back a long, <i>long</i> way. There are some witches who don't mind cavorting with the Abe when a good party is on the horizon, but the Abe cells in Boston prefer to have more fascinating &quot;guests&quot; brought in from elsewhere rather than risk their necks and standing in the wake of possible murder charges.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron Group: Scouting:</b> Seeing some of the nation's best medical professionals graduating from the city, Cheiron's regional office is quick to snap anyone with real potential away before Null Mysteriis can continue to use them. No one knows what Cheiron's overall goal in Boston is, but rumors are spreading that the hope is to find a sure-fire piece of a witch that can actually convey full magic power to their hunters.<br /> <br /> <b>Division Six: Purging:</b> Division Six's presence in the city isn't firmly established in terms of how many cells they have present, but they have enough that the witches play hell trying to root them out. Many carbombs and shootings blamed on the city's organized crime presence were more likely the work of 6's witch hunters, though in recent years with the fall from grace of groups like the Winter Hill Gang the group has decided to shift from outright violence to more subtle means of elimination like computer fraud and what has essentially become &quot;identity destruction&quot;, though the stories on the street also claim that the group is actively kidnapping reality deviants to secret labs for unknown research.<br /> <br /> <b>The Hunt Club: Contemplative:</b> With a relatively underpopulated clubhouse in the city, the Hunt Club in Boston is still enough of an established set that their preferred rules have become part of the group's overall ethos. Inadvertently aiding the authorities in clearing out many of the gangs after Whitey Bulger's escape, the Boston Rules set of the Hunt Club have begun to wonder if perhaps the worst witches might be their next series of targets after all.<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of Saint George: Warded:</b> Present since the very founding of the city, the Knights have had a Shadow Court in place on what they claim is a place that the witches once managed to summon up one of the faceless angels. Though firmly emplaced, the Knights know that the witches are still in control of the city as a whole, and so have made sure that their safehouses are as protected as possible. When the knights go to do battle, they roll hard.<br /> <br /> <b>The Long Night: Small:</b> As a city essentially built on Catholicism, Boston had only small space to offer when the Long Night came to the city. This isn't to say the group isn't still a known part of the city's hunter community, but their small numbers and relatively low profile keep the Long Night close to their own territories most nights.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule: Scouring:</b> The Loyalists, like the AKD, comb through the city each night to find any more evidence of occult secrets left behind by the Founding Fathers, feeling that there may still be more in the city and in Boston Harbor that they could use for their own goals. The Three Old Men themselves have given their approval for greater backing to be given to the Loyalists, to grab as much as possible from the region, thoguh unlike the AKD no one has heard anything about a time table.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge: Established:</b> Like the Abbey, the Lucifuge has had a place in Boston for many years. Though they consistently deny any association with <i>any</i> part of the Kennedy family, they do have their blood in several Brahmin names, including the Cabots, Dwights, Lodges, and Tudors. This allows the cells in Boston to take their time with any problems. After all, they have more than enough money combined to bounce back from any difficulty.<br /> <br /> <b>Maiden's Blood Sisterhood: Open:</b> The Sisterhood's opinion on witchcraft what it is, the group has opened several lines of communication between the witches and other hunters who might want to work out arrangements and deals. Though vampires are present in Boston, the Sisterhood has such a strong presence in the city's universities that the leeches prefer to steer clear, allowing the Sisterhood to become a valuable part of the hunter community for a change rather than a side note.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum: Firm:</b> Boston isn't run by the Irish anymore, but it certainly has more than enough families in the working neighborhoods willing to go to bat for the Church. Holding a firm grip on Southie and acting as the home city of Archbishop Gallaher himself, the Malleus have broken several covens over the 20th century and have forced many more witches to give up their arcane powers for good. No one sees this changing anytime soon, especially after the Malleus wiped out some kind of witch cult disguised as an offshoot of the Church.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero: Rolling:</b> With conflict practically every night, Network Zero's Boston cells are essentially overwhelmed with footage of witches and hunters using amazing magical abilities to get a leg up against each other. Footage out of Boston always gets high views and sharing numbers, but the age old problem of cries of fake footage always keep the wider world from realizing what they're actually seeing.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis: Pushing:</b> Unlike many cities, cells for ORAS in Boston are continually going out each night to find out more about the witches that surround them. Able to recruit from some of the best colleges in the nation, the issue is that many older members are typically strictly Rationalist, while the younger generation is almost always willing to dabble in the Open-Minds area of study. At times this has even spread to the classroom, leaving many feeling that the Boston cells are in danger of an old vs young showdown.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean Brotherhood: Underground: </b>Even for hunters, the Brotherhood's cells in Boston are currently laying low. Knowing that the witches would purge the city to keep from losing their power, the Brotherhood are scouting out witch gathering points and several smaller covens. The hope is that by keeping the herd from getting spooked, the Brotherhood can build their strength quickly enough to start taking on the more powerful, and therefore more magic-filled witches.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE: Distant:</b> Though possessing several of the nation's most vital colleges, TFV has moved away from the city since the infiltration of the FBI field office by the Winter Hill Gang was handled. Yet rumors persist that there's at least two cells in the city that &quot;everyone&quot; knows about. One keeps people away from the historic buildings that served as hotspots of revolutionary activity, the other actively going between these buildings as if they're looking for something.<br /> <br /> <b>Union: Firm:</b> The Union has several strong cells in the Boston area, made up of the same blue-collar workers that the Union was started by. Controlling the docks with an iron grip, the Union is reasonably willing to parlay with the witches so long as the fighting is kept away from kids and residential neighborhoods. Unfortunately, several witch covens have reportedly been making strikes to test the docks, and the Union is getting antsy about their &quot;friendly&quot; witches getting their people under control.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU: </b><b>Underwhelming:</b> Assigning several agents to the Boston field office, VASCU in Boston is typically just seconded to the office for typical agent duties. Yet the VASCU agents are consistently considered a danger by local witches, who claim that their &quot;magic&quot; is somehow wrong or false. The VASCU agents have no idea what any of it means, but to their ears it sounds like they might be edging in on a racket the witches don't want to lose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 11-11-2016, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T14:08:26-08:00","id":1000426,"title":"","content":"A coven of witches are trying to take over the Boston drugs market and are selling drugs with magical effects, that's two direct conflicts of interest with the Ascending Ones.<br /> <br /> Panopticon has a seperate programme to D6 in Boston who focus on reserching reality deviants and how to counteract them. Sometimes D6 cells are requested to deliver live witches to it.<br /> <br /> The Knights of St. George have been here almost as long as the city has. They had their Shadow Court at Salem, which is coincidently on the spot that some witches summoned what sounds like a Faceless Angel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T18:26:16-08:00","id":1000566,"title":"","content":"A couple of things to note for Denver is that there's a vampire-hunting pack active in the area, that it's one of the most united places in the country for Forsaken, and that wolves are very high up in the city's power chain. There are also monstrous dinosaur- and prehistoric animal-spirit hybrids roaming the local Shadow, trying to find Essence they can still consume and failing miserably. Think Jurassic Park meets Frankenstein.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T14:55:53-08:00","id":1001000,"title":"","content":"For New Orleans I'd be really tempted to alter the setting. I mean, the book was released just prior to Katrina for one.<br /> <br /> However, if you ever read the original demo for Requiem, there's an interesting chapter where a Morbus effectively commits an act of bio-terrorism in the French Quarter. A treatable but still highly fatal disease breaks out and there are wide spread reports of mysterious smears of blood being found which then disappear with the sun rise... It wasn't exactly subtle.<br /> <br /> Katrina is an opportunity unlike pretty much anything else for Valkyrie. There are usually limits to what they can reasonably deploy on the streets of the US; but when there are tens of thousands of mobilised troops who's going to notice a couple of hundred TWILIGHT kill teams?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T09:20:11-08:00","id":1001376,"title":"","content":"<b>Detroit: Unliving it Up</b><br /> <br /> The Motor City has been plagued in recent years by more than just closing factories and urban decay. Undead beasts made of reused human bodies have begun to consider the city some kind of gathering point, and their strange magics have not helped the regional situation. Now as the urban jungle continues to become overgrown and neighborhoods are literally barricaded from the rest of the city, the hunters in the region have to make a hard choice between the Vigil and simply surviving.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones: Supportive:</b> For many neighborhoods, the Ascending Ones are actually the closest thing to an infrastructure they have. Able to provide food to those truly in need, organizing community clothing and medical drives, and even taking steps to try and break down the barricades that close off these neighborhoods from the city, the Cult of the Phoenix also ensures that these neighborhoods are hooked on the drugs they supply. Overall however, the goal is to capture the strange walking dead men and take the alchemical magic they somehow possess.<br /> <br /> <b>The Cheiron Group: Pursuing:</b> Lakeshore Biotechnic sees the undead things as vital to securing several new forms of thaumatech as well as established ones. Scouring the city nightly, Lakeshore cells grab where they can, popping massive amounts of medication to fight off the effects of the uncanny valley effect the thing have on mankind. It doesn't always work though, and more than once a cell has been reprimanded because the body was dead by the time it came back.<br /> <br /> <b>The Long Night: Surging:</b> With churches and missions across the city able to give hope to those greatest in need, Long Night-affiliated congregations are the most numerous cells in the city. Unfortunately, the magics surrounding the undead humans walking through the city turn the sometimes peaceful Long Night into a raging inferno of righteous hatred.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule: Laying Low:</b> Despite the typically high Germanic population in the Midwest, the Loyalists have little to find in Detroit that would be useful to them. The city itself isn't so ancient as to hide any occult secrets, and the dead men walking about don't usually know anything useful to their goals. There are, however, rumors that the Loyalists are actually keeping a very close eye on several art museums that now have in their possession several statues that reportedly are cursed, and even allegedly move when no one is looking.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge: Scrambling:</b> With such desperation, demons find fertile grounds to make deals in Detroit. From executives trying to save their own skins to mothers and fathers trying to feed their families for another day. As with Denver, they only have a single cell in the region to work with, but instead of followers the cell instead prefers to use several independent cells in return for the Lucifuge eliminating several gangs in the city wreaking havoc. The irony wasn't lost.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum: Supporting:</b> Instead of trying to find monsters or purge the wicked, the Sisterhood of St. Wisdom runs the Detroit operations of the Inquisition. Knowing that a hungry mouth invites temptation, the Malleus are focused on several community outreach efforts aimed at keeping the city from becoming too desperate to control. So far it's helped, and as long as the leading Mother Superior can stand to ignore the Lucifuge's actions, they can focus on those most in need.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero: Hardened:</b> In a city like Detroit, the Netzos have to adapt or die. Often as skilled with a gun as their cameras, Detroit is considered the place for the hardest Network Zero cells to go to prove themselves. The group has actually proven itself relatively useful for a change, filming several crimes in progress that have helped the city's prosecutor nail multiple dangerous criminals. More important to their own ends, the group has sat down with several of the dead men, interviewing them about what they are, what they're trying to do, and why Detroit is so important. Spreading this information about, the Network has managed to at least help multiple cells in the region understand just what they're getting into.<br /> <br /> <b>Night Watch: At War:</b> Seeing the Ascending Ones and gangs dragging their city further and further down, the Watch has decided that they must fight all-out against them. The Watch in Detroit are heavily armed at all times and never unprepared for a fight. While Philadelphia is nearly-constantly under threat of a hunter civil war breaking out between all groups in the city, the Watch in Detroit is solely focused on the gangs and their suppliers in the Ascending Ones. Of course, trying to take on a conspiracy is a difficult prospect in the best of times, and the neighborhoods the Watch has are quickly becoming overwhelmed by drugs and a lack of attention from the city worse than before.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis: Tearing Hair Out:</b> The undead things would advance several dozen disciplines overnight, but the problem is that they almost seem to have some kind of personal entropy field surrounding them that wreaks havoc with lab equipment and even just trying to stay focused on the task at hand. Multiple other Null Mysteriis experts in the region are showing worrying obsession with recreating these creatures, and their cellmates have only just barely managed to hold them back from going full-bore Frankenstein.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE: Researching:</b> The Task Force doesn't have an active, get-out-and-kill group of cells in Detroit. The focus is instead on R&amp;D, using the city's existing &quot;abandoned&quot; infrastructure to develop several technologies that might aid in reclaiming the city from the undead freaks. Though secret, TFV researchers are finding that the monsters do have <i>something</i> inside them, and that something could be very useful.<br /> <br /> <b>The Union:</b> <b>Struggling:</b> The once-mighty UAW has come to face the fact that Detroit is flagging harder than ever. Still, the Union cells in the city and suburbs aren't giving up yet. They know the undead creatures are part of the problem, and so they have made it a mission to find them and kill them. With a high proportion of General Strike-affiliated cells in the area and firm control of the three remaining auto plants, the Union in Detroit is extremely proactive against any threats. However, they also have had several confrontations between themselves and the militant Night Watch.<br /> <br /> <b>Utopia Now: Plotting:</b> Seeing Detroit as the perfect place to unveil their plans, Utopia Now has a cell in the region ready to recreate the heydays of Detroit steel and the Motor City. Readying the opening of an independent automotive plant in the city capable of becoming competition with newer companies like Tesla, Utopia Now is having a hell of a time trying to make sure the undead things don't ruin their plans.<br /> <br /> (Don't worry Kings, I'll write up a Princess Detroit too)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T22:53:53-08:00","id":1001635,"title":"","content":"<b>Miami: A Beautiful Madness</b><br /> <br /> A city in danger of sinking, Miami is still home of one of the largest accepted populations of fairies in the US today. This has turned the city into a dangerous place, as the legendary mask hiding the fairies makes it nigh-impossible for your average hunter to actually know who they're hunting at all. Fortunately, the city's fairies are often so overt in how they act that a little observation goes a long way.<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey: Don't Ask:</b> Really, don't. No one in the Miami vigil wants to even imagine what debauched heights the Abe is capable of getting itself up to in the city.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru, Ascending Ones: Buying:</b> With so many fairy relics and goblin fruits in the city's markets, both of these ancient cults go out of their way to stock up when they can. Unfortunately, many believe this is actually putting their cells in the city more and more under the control of the fairies rather than preventing further trouble.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron Group: Frustrated:</b> As in their other operations, Cheiron's regional subsidiary Iberria Health Solutions is terrible at bringing in fairies. Fortunately for the rest of the world, they have a plan to work against the fairies by exploiting what seems to be a fairy weakness for rescuing kidnap victims. Orchestrating several kidnappings, Iberria has found at least one genuine fairy that was made out of metal and calling out how it wouldn't be a steel beam again. It was right, because it became a series of possible implants instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Illuminated Brotherhood: Exploring:</b> With the sheer amount of drugs the Brotherhood takes just to experience the spirit world, it doesn't surprise many when they found fairies in Miami. But it has also twisted the local spiritual landscape, with spirits unlike any they've seen before reflecting old and modern fairy tails. Thinking there's got to be a connection, the Brotherhood wants to learn as much as it can about these &quot;fairies&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>The Long Night: Comforting:</b> Most of the fairies report terrible, literally inhuman abuses from their time in a place called &quot;Arcadia&quot;. Taking these shattered souls into their care, the Long Night has tried continually to heal the wounds they can. This has made the Long Night strange bedfellows with the regional fairy power structure, meaning the Long Night actually has extra protection from several groups of fairies.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule: Testing: </b>The old fairy tales are wrong in so many ways that the Loyalists are using Miami as a test bed to find out for sure what does and doesn't work. To that goal they've devoted considerable resources in terms of manpower and capital. Iron does have an effect, fairies are utterly bound by agreements, but that's about it. Some are harmed by church bells and religious icons, others gleefully dance about in churches, during the mass even! All the Loyalists really have to work with at this point are the unpublished drafts of the Brothers Grimm.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge: Lost:</b> As much as they know they're royalty to the demons of Hell, the fairies of Miami don't see the Lucifuge as kindred spirits. Rather, several groups of fairies have actually tried to kill Lucifuge members claiming something about privateers. The term implies some some of organized group of mercenaries, and the Lucifuge has taken this as a sign that the fairies might actually be fighting one another in the city at the present.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum: Worn:</b> If it isn't fairies <i>not</i> running from churchbells, it's the people gone mad from them in their wake. The Church has resources, but Miami's churches are busy with the day to day lives of human beings, meaning that changelings coming for help will typically only be there to feed on emotion or make things worse to accomplish the former. With such foes, the Malleus in the city are being worn down more and more by the fae.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero: Frazzled:</b> The cells of Network Zero are absolutely done trying to find fairies in Miami. With the Mask able to shield fairies from AV equipment as well as human sight, the Secret Frequency has decided to instead strike out looking for the Goblin Markets, looking for a camera that could actually breach the Mask. The idea being if they can find such an object anywhere, it would have to be at these secret swap meets.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis: Done:</b> Even the Open-Minds of Null Mysteriis have had enough of Miami's fairy power structure. From raids made on labs to toying with their goals, the Misties are ready to pack up and leave the city for good after everything that's happened to them. Unfortunately one group of changelings, believing they see like-minded &quot;occultists&quot; in the organization, are trying to entice them to stay with offers to drop the mask and help them see the truth. The Misties are ready to turn their contact information over to the more militant hunters out of sheer frustration.<br /> <br /> <b>Talbot Group: Expanding:</b> The Talbot Group only recently opened up a center in Miami, and for them changelings are entirely different psychoses all together. Suffering from what they've started calling Compound-PTSD, the Talbot center is trying to gently offer new help to the changeling society. A small group of half a dozen changelings have decided to accept the offer of help, but threats what must be the wider changeling community keep coming. This has forced the group to offer free counseling services to hunters in return for protection. With few therapists actually capable of understanding their struggle, it's one of the best protected buildings in the city from anything. It also raises question as to why the Long Night is somehow okay, but the Group isn't.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE: Trapping:</b> Fairies and other dimensions are apparently high on TFV's watchlist, and reports continue to circulate through the hunter community that the MIBs are kidnapping fairies where they can find them, dosing them with knockout drugs and putting them under intense guards. Of course, no one actually knows why.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU: Searching: </b>Kidnappings fall under FBI jurisdiction, and in Miami there's plenty to go around. Adding in VASCU cells due to the need for manpower, the agents are troubled by the sheer collective mental instability that permeates the city. This hasn't taken away from their duty however, but the &quot;fairy&quot; kidnappers and the few returned victims seem to have disturbingly similar mental patterns.<br /> <br /> <b>Union: Rising:</b> With a strong blue collar workforce in the city's neighborhoods, the Union has already scouted several individuals that could be valuable new members. One group of workers in the city's water and power department in particular are making waves as becoming suspicious about what lurks in the shadows. The Union is preparing to make moves against the fairies, and they aren't going to make any bad deals this time. In this strike, the powers that be will not sway the workers as far as the Union sees it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 11-11-2016, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T02:23:39-08:00","id":1001685,"title":"","content":"really good stuff you have here. I like it all. Are you going to later add the US 2E settings as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T21:18:05-08:00","id":1002103,"title":"","content":"If I knew which cities they were.<br /> <br /> <b>New York City: Grim Grinning Ghosts</b><br /> <br /> The Big Apple has some of the most diverse hunters present anywhere in the world. Practically ever major US compact and several conspiracies have cells in the city alongside with lone cells from the various neighborhoods. Rumors still persist that there is some kind of &quot;ultra-conspiracy&quot; in the UN itself, controlling the conspiracies and compacts of several international governments, but those are at best conspiracy theories. The more pertinent problem are ghosts of a city that never sleeps. New York is crawling with ghosts, meaning that instead of trying to kill something nearly all cells have to make something either accept that it's dead or force it to move on.<br /> <br /> <b>Ahl al-Jabal: Swift: </b>Focused on keeping the vampiric population under control, the compact is able to use the sheer size of New York's population to flit from neighborhood to neighborhood as they carry out their mission. Most other hunters are fine with this, as it keeps them focused on their goal of handling the ghosts.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru: Careful:</b> The Shield and the Spear moves with caution in New York. The city is home to one of their largest relic vaults in the continent, and much of their efforts are focused on warding it against intrusion by the local witches. This, in addition to the abundance of ghosts Ghostwalkers, forces the conspiracy's hunters to take up a defensive Vigil built on observation and subterfuge.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones:<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey: Nervous: </b>The New York Abe are getting worried about how many ghosts are in the city lately. The 1970s were a wild time, and a lot of blood was spilled because of the Abbey's actions. Blood from hunters, monsters, <i>and</i> civilians. Worried that some hunters are going to find out exactly what happened, the Abbey has started calling in dozens of exorcists and spiritualists from outside to try and clean house.<br /> <br /> <b>Barrett Commission: Balancing: </b>Since New York's civil government literally rivals several small nations, the Commission found little trouble worming into relatively small but invaluable positions high in the chain. Being so highly placed and in the know, the Commission has become a kind of moderating force on the rest of the city's hunters, handling disputes involving territory, calling in markers, and generally trying to make sure the Vigil runs smoothly without the big guns getting involved.<br /> <br /> <b>Cainite Heresy: Stunted: </b>Without the number of vampires found in other cities coupled with the willingness of hunters in New York to at the very least tolerate each other, the Cainites have been left in a city where they can barely move. Habibti Ma is especially on guard against them, seeing them as a dangerous cult. The Cainites are therefore convinced that H.B. is a front for vampires trying to stop them, and are readying to take them out.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron Group: Earning:</b> Ghosts can be profitable, but now overtly so like vampires or other strange creatures. So for now, Cheiron in New York is actually doing something no one can believe; acting as a legitimate pharmaceutical corporation with proper human testing laws being followed and all reports going to the FDA. Which is why everyone is so freaking suspicious of them.<br /> <br /> <b>Division Six: Useless:</b> So focused on witches, Division Six cells that form in New York are left flat-footed when the &quot;witches&quot; don't die while they're being shot. Losing multiple cells over the years, Division Six has become a laughing stock among New York's hunter community. Even the latest cell has come to accept this, working instead of try and make a database of the various witches in the city rather than get themselves kill. Unfortunately, Mr. Jones is growing impatient.<br /> <br /> <b>Faithful of Shulpae: Cannibalistic:</b> The cult's followers in New York have long hunted Ghostwalkers for their Feasts, taking their power over the dead for themselves. But now, they turn on each other even as the ghosts of their previous meals come to haunt them. One of them, in particular, had been a necromancer in life, and he has used his magic to direct his fellow shades against their killers. Some of the Faithful killed by them returned to life through the Bargain, but their second chance is more often than not plagued with danger from their former compatriots more than any other threat.<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of St. Adrian:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Knights of St. George: Purged:</b> Given their interest in the leylines of the city, New York's witches do not take kindly to the Knights' presence. Whatever foothold the conspiracy had was quickly destroyed through their efforts, and the few who managed to escape alive are left operating alone or in pairs. These survivors work to keep each other updated on the witches' movements, but they have recently begun coordinating their efforts for a strike against one of the less organized covens.<br /> <br /> <b>Greenwich Village Irregulars: Symbolic:</b> Having grown into a compact since the 1970s, the Irregulars stand as an example of what New York hunters have accomplished compared to their more territorial compatriots in Philadelphia. Keeping the pulse on the city's hunters from the ground, the Irregulars are now taking the unusual step of trying to contact the fog-men to see if there can't be a possible peace between the two groups.<br /> <br /> <b>Habibti Ma: Guarding:</b> In a city the size of New York, Habibti Ma stands vigil over the outcast and neglected. Perfect targets of cults and dangerous groups, Habibti Ma has made it a focus to interfere as much as possible with cult recruiters as well as pushing journalists and police to keep a closer eye on several &quot;death cults&quot; in the city.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunt Club: Safe: </b>With the richer neighborhoods practically cities within a city, the Hunt Club is ensconced in it's own personal security bubble surrounded by private guards, the police, and plenty of ground to cover. So safely, they've granted their title of &quot;Long Island Serial Killer&quot; to a younger member, hoping they'll be up to carrying on the cat and mouse game with the NYPD on the Long Island beaches.<br /> <br /> <b>Illuminated Brotherhood:<br /> <br /> Les Mysteries: Protected: </b>The fog-men are convinced Les Mysteries are being used by ghosts and spirits, and technically they are right. What they never quite understand is that the ghosts and spirits associated with Les Mysteries are actually willing partners most of the time. This has protected the group's mediums and spiritualists, but for how long is up for debate.<br /> <br /> <b>Long Night: Evangelizing:</b> Pushing out into the city with pamphlets by day and weapons by night, the dozens of Long Night cells in New York believe that God has granted them a sacred duty to clear out a modern day Gomorrah. Believing that New York will be the start of their glorious rapture, the Long Night are trying desperately to bring in more and more followers to their cause. Unfortunately, several cells have tactics and attitudes on recruits and converts that run right into the sights of Habibti Ma.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule: Gathering:</b> The Loyalists seek out the ghosts of New York to find information. Information on where the bodies might be buried, on who the killer is, on what it is under the floor I'm standing on that you died for. This has brought the Loyalists into contact most often with the &quot;fog-men&quot;, or sin-eaters who consider the city theirs. Fortunately, the fog-men are more concerned with getting ghosts to move on, and the Loyalists taking away any anchors makes the relationship that much more cordial.<br /> <br /> <b>Maiden's Blood Sisterhood: Closed off:</b> Not willing to let any local vampires get their fangs into their campuses, the Sisterhood doesn't have many experts on ghosts to call on. What they know for sure is that several of their members have come back after death, and not knowing what to do about them has literally put the group into limbo over what to do about them.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero: Downcast:</b> Surprisingly, many NetZo cells in New York City are anxious about their situation. While fully capable of filming brilliant footage of haunted buildings and unquiet ghosts, the sheer amount of noise coming from reality TV shows purporting to explore the exact same phenomena means that even if a great video is put out, it's compared to the reality TV garbage everywhere else. Ghosts used to be one of Network Zero's biggest tools, but now many fear they're a liability.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis: Studying:</b> Rather than worry about doctrinal squabbles like in Boston, ORAS HQ in New York is more focused on more attainable scientific goals. Instead of trying to explain ghosts or find their origins, the Misties are just trying to come up with better ways to find and communicate with them. Once a clear line of communication is established both ways, then the real work can begin.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean Brotherhood: Moving:</b> The Brotherhood has killed several fog-men and rituals using the Rite of Hecate, and with it the fog-men they've killed have stayed dead. Of course, given the purpose of the murders, the Brotherhood has preferred to keep this little revelation to themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Talbot Group: Listening:</b> With so many hunters in the city, the Talbot Group center is their port of call when they desperately need someone to talk to. The Talbots offer a willing ear to listen to many of these hunters, as well as a support system for victims of everything from possession to ghouling to witch mind control.<br /> <br /> <b>Union: Strong:</b> The many neighborhoods of New York are filled with working families, and as such as home to dozens of Union cells. Holding firm to the principles that strong neighborhoods make strong protections against monsters, most Union cells in New York are pretty quick to send out a call for assistance if they're facing down a haunting that's tougher to deal with than a quick blessing with sage and kindly asking the spirit to leave.<br /> <br /> <b>Utopia Now: Scheming:</b> Mostly coming out of Wall Street, the cells of Utopia Now don't have time for all the namby-pamby feel good times that other New York cells experience. Instead, Utopia Now is planning to open up competition to the NY Stock Exchange using their finds. Their hope is that with the bio-tech they have, they can make new trading algorithms and systems that would literally blow the market wide open. Ghosts? Who cares.<br /> <br /> <b>WIP</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 11-21-2016, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T05:47:05-08:00","id":1002508,"title":"","content":"Suggestion for Aegis in New York, somewhat inspired by the Doctor Strange movie.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru: Careful:</b> The Shield and the Spear moves with caution in New York. The city is home to one of their largest relic vaults in the continent, and much of their efforts are focused on warding it against intrusion by the local witches. This, in addition to the abundance of ghosts Ghostwalkers, forces the conspiracy's hunters to take up a defensive Vigil built on observation and subterfuge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T10:44:32-08:00","id":1002557,"title":"","content":"New York also has a lot of Awakened. It's not a setting but it's referred to as having a population too big for the consilium to properly manage.<br /> <br /> I'd suspect New York is probably the kind of place where where every supernatural population is well represented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T04:45:46-08:00","id":1002831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1002557#post1002557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New York also has a lot of Awakened. It's not a setting but it's referred to as having a population too big for the consilium to properly manage.<br /> <br /> I'd suspect New York is probably the kind of place where where every supernatural population is well represented.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall a Nameless Order being written up on one of the 1E blue books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T05:08:03-08:00","id":1002836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1002831#post1002831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I recall a Nameless Order being written up on one of the 1E blue books.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is in Left Handed Path, I believe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T10:25:29-08:00","id":1003467,"title":"","content":"<b>Washington DC: Dying is Easy, Governing Isn't</b><br /> <br /> As the seat of power for the most powerful nation on Earth, Washington DC is constantly being played by every possible faction of creatures which think they can control the lives of men. Unfortunately, such a city means every conspiracy on Earth has a presence there as well, including several conspiracies from other nations embedded in their nation's embassies. For now, DC remains relatively secured from the supernatural. How long this can last when the regular political climate is in such upheaval, no one can say.<br /> <br /> <b>Ahl al-Jabal:</b> <b>Quiet:</b> The hashashin primarily patrol the city's neighborhoods, and aside from an occasional rogue leech there is little for the compact to do other than be wary and ready.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru: Walking the Labyrinth:</b> As the conspiracies claim, DC is laid out in an unusual fashion, and the Spear and Shield use it as the perfect test for their initiates. Drugging them up and letting them loose, these would-be guardians must seek out the occult mysteries laid out in the city, trekking through the mall to uncover the truths their masters would so desperately want them to uncover.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones: Gutted:</b> The Cult of the Phoenix was hit by a one-two punch in the beginning of the 21st century. First there was Ronnie's War on Drugs, which only fractured the hold the Ascending Ones had on the city's drug trade. Second was the 9/11, which allowed the government's monster hunters to smash hard on their other enemies as &quot;domestic enemy agents&quot;. Reeling, the Ascending Ones keep their heads low in the nation's capitol.<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey:</b><b> Bored:</b> The DC Abe franchise is just...bored. The city is so well protected there's nothing to do, and even with fresh &quot;entertainers&quot; shipped in from out of the area the presence of both dozens of conspiracies <i>and</i> mundane Federal law enforcement means that the Abbey in DC is hemorrhaging members, and some inside fear it may even shut down entirely. Not a bad sign for the rest of the hunter community however.<br /> <br /> <b>Barrett Commission: Everywhere:</b> DC is the Commission's town, the place where it made its bones on the blood of vampires. Patrolling Congress, the Pentagon, and the lobbyists on K Street, the Commission is still stymied at every turn by the powerful conspiracies that block them from finding out what they most vitally need. Including trying to finally break through the information stonewall surrounding &quot;VALKYRIE&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Cainite Heresy: Trouble:</b> As a cult convinced that vampires control everything, the Cainites see DC as one of their most obvious targets to hit. Of course, with the sheer security surrounding the city, they're typically stopped before anything even starts. So now the Cainites are starting to hit the <i>conspiracies</i> before they go after the government. Because after all, it's not like this won't raise more trouble down the line. Right? Right.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron Group: Quiet:</b> The Cheiron Group only has a corporate office in the city, with the majority of their lobbying done through a K Street firm that specializes in pharma lobbying. There's only a single cell in the city, charged with keeping an eye on the office. Meaning that Cheiron simply does business in Washington DC, no &quot;side projects&quot; allowed.<br /> <br /> <b>Division Six: Concealed:</b> Safely hidden in the shadows of the bigger players, Six is presently making hits on members of the Aegis Kai Doru, told by Mr. Jones that these &quot;users&quot; are on the path to potentially <i>becoming</i> reality deviants. Something the Division desperately can't allow. Operating out of the Smithsonian under the guise of &quot;government contractors&quot;, the Division is presently hitting whenever a potential member of the &quot;cult&quot; strikes out on the Mall at night.<br /> <br /> <b>Faithful of Shulpae: Prowling:</b> While they face the same difficulties as the Abbey and the Hunt Club, the Faithful linger in DC like moths to a flame. They suspect that gods are flocking to the city, and the few local Guides they have eagerly seek further proof of this. While other hunters have yet to take notice of these activities, their vigilance against supernatural incursion means it is only a matter of time.<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of St. George:</b><b> Stockpiling:</b> When the threat of the 1976 Bicentennial War was revealed, the Knights stepped up actions within the city proper. Fortunately for those inside the city, the early cells of Division Six had already done a good deal of heavy lifting, leaving the knights to continue preparations. 2076 will be here sooner than anyone will realize.<br /> <br /> <b>Habibti Ma: Pushing:</b> The families of the group have noticed that many of their lost loved ones seem to turn up in Washington DC without fail, and so have set themselves up in the area in an effort to both save the lost and lobby Congress. Operating right across the street from the city's Scientology office as a giant &quot;Up Yours&quot; to cults across the city, the group is presently lobbying the House for a bill that would increase the ability of law enforcement to crack down on dangerous cults.<br /> <br /> <b>The Hunt Club: Pre-Occupied:</b> Like the Abbey, the Hunt Club is careful where it steps in DC. No matter their connections, the fact is the group can't dare risk being found out because a senator from Kentucky got caught with the entrails of a call-girl in his hands. Some in the city have even suggested sticking to the Boston rules in the city permanently, which has soaked up a lot of the group's energy.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule: Seeking:</b> Despite not being one of the older cities in the US, Washington is a massive hub of esoteric material and information. Coupled with the Nazis brought into the nation during the heyday of Operation PAPERCLIP, the Loyalists have spent too many nights in Washington seeking out the secrets of their own past and the hidden pieces of America's history.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge: Stalking:</b> How many times has someone believed some politicians are just too lucky to be just coincidence? That they must've made some kind of deal for their good fortune and power. The members of the Lucifuge know too well that this is true frighteningly often, though they think that the Kennedy and Bush families actually <i>do</i> just have damn good luck (for what that might be worth). As far as the Seventh Generation is concerned, their duty in Washington DC is to watch the halls of power for corruption of the demonic kind. Even they don't think they have the capabilities to go after the sheer amount of bribery and back-scratching in DC.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum: Meditating:</b> Though the city is considered quiet to many hunters, the Malleus still feels that there is always a potential threat somewhere waiting for the right trigger. As Gallaher is preoccupied on personal projects, the DC Malleus cells consider it a more important duty to make sure that the vampires aren't making powerful necks into dinner. So they practice with their benedictions, studying them to learn to more effectively use them when the time so rarely does come.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero: Problematic:</b> While most hunters don't mind Network Zero in terms of principle, in DC the Secret Frequency are downright despised. The fact is that the function of government actually takes place in those oft-hated smoke filled rooms and back alleyways because those are the places you can speak frankly enough to get your actual points across. So when Network Zero is constantly bugging offices and those same back alleys, people get upset.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis: Distant:</b> Though at one time having a respectable presence in the capitol, in modern nights Null Mysteriis has come to see Washington DC as a sort of lost cause. Too much political action and a growing sense that scientific inquiry isn't as important as figuring out what special interest gets the next years funding has made many members of ORAS leave and seek greener pastures, leaving those who remain simply carrying on in their own way.<br /> <br /> <b>Tastk Force: VALKYRIE: Ruling:</b> The Commission may be established, but TFV runs DC. No one moves without them knowing it, hits without them feeling it, or talks without them listening. Apart from essentially culling the Ascending Ones in the past three decades, they've kept Network Zero in (relative) check and have fought off actions by the Cainites for seven years. The salad days might be over soon however, as more and more regional TFV commands are becoming stretched to breaking point.<br /> <br /> <b>Union: Hemmed In:</b> If the regular workers of the city were to decide they'd had enough, every function of government would essentially cease. So Washington DC is actually considered a town relatively hostile to labor causes. This has made the Union in the city feel as though they're being pressured by the monsters controlling the government, turning many Union cells in the city to the arms of the Political faction.<br /> <br /> <b>Utopia Now: Lobbying:</b> Where Habibti Ma is simply pushing for a single bill, Utopia Now is trying to get sweeping legislation passed that would make it simpler than ever to accomplish their goal. When it's pointed out they're using their hated enemy to accomplish their goals in their favor, Utopia Now cells brush it off as simply &quot;using a resource&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU: Operating:</b> In their home city, VASCU wants to focus on perfectly explainable and (somewhat) mundane crimes and felonies. The FBI has too many senior agents sending more &quot;curious&quot; agents to the basement with the lunatics for anyone in VASCU to feel comfortable to mention some of the things they've &quot;heard&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 11-21-2016, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:30:57-08:00","id":1005017,"title":"","content":"In my own DC setting I have the Ascending Ones as a formerly powerful Conspiracy in the District who's influence has largely been dismantled. They accrued a great deal of strength by piggybacking on various secret societies and cults of Egyptian sacred geometry that used to be much more prominent in the city, while also having hands in radical black politics and esoteric Africana. Times changed though. Their traditional sources of power gradually diminished, then finally the war on drugs and the war on terror dealt them a one-two punch as TFV used the crack epidemic and 9/11 to bring the hammer down on their activities to the point that the AO are only a shadow of their former selves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T14:27:38-08:00","id":1005856,"title":"","content":"Idea based on what I skimmed from Cursed Necropolis: DC.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Faithful of Shulpae: Prowling:</b> While they face the same difficulties as the Abbey and the Hunt Club, the Faithful linger in DC like moths to a flame. They suspect that gods are flocking to the city, and the few local Guides they have eagerly seek further proof of this. While other hunters have yet to take notice of these activities, their vigilance against supernatural incursion means it is only a matter of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T15:37:19-08:00","id":1005887,"title":"","content":"For the Aegis and the Ascending Ones in New Orleans.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru: Seeking:</b> Faced with a well-established presence of local witches, shapeshifters, and vampires, the Aegis operated in New Orleans with a light touch. Individual cells tend to focus their efforts at locating and acquiring any relics as discretely and quickly as possible. While the years that followed Hurricane Katrina allowed them to secure a few notable items of power, the conspiracy remains a small group in the city.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones: Syncretized:</b> Like the Ahl al-Jabal, the Cult of the Phoenix does not identify too strongly with Islam to avoid painting a target on for the vampires. Their cell in New Orleans was greatly influenced by the local culture, though, to the point that elements of Voodoo were woven into their predominantly Christian practices. Louisiana's Ascending Ones thus tend to use their Elixirs to imbue an assortment of artifacts and charms rather than directly imbibing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T15:57:15-08:00","id":1005890,"title":"","content":"And for the Faithful in New York.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Faithful of Shulpae: Cannibalistic:</b> The cult's followers in New York have long hunted Ghostwalkers for their Feasts, taking their power over the dead for themselves. But now, they turn on each other even as the ghosts of their previous meals come to haunt them. One of them, in particular, had been a necromancer in life, and he has used his magic to direct his fellow shades against their killers. Some of the Faithful killed by them returned to life through the Bargain, but their second chance is more often than not plagued with danger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T22:34:50-08:00","id":1006000,"title":"","content":"Entry for Detroit, with a reference to Werewolf 2E.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru: Scouring:</b> The Rock City is a hotspot for the conspiracy, both for its werewolf population and the influx of Reanimated. They know that many of the former are involved in Detroit's decline, and that some of their kind are working with a group of local hunters to oppose their efforts. The latter, however, draws much of their attention, as they've pieced together why they gather in such large numbers. Several cells have managed to claim a few relics keyed specifically to the Reanimated, and many more are believed to be scattered all over the area. Furthermore, at least one of these relics may be crippling the city as badly as the werewolves. Armed with this knowledge, the Shield and the Spear is scrambling to gather as much of these items as they can while destroying the rest that remain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-21-2016, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T23:07:13-08:00","id":1006014,"title":"","content":"New York entry.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of St. George: Purged:</b> Given their interest in the leylines of the city, New York's witches do not take kindly to the Knights' presence. Whatever foothold the conspiracy had was quickly destroyed through their efforts, and the few who managed to escape alive are left operating alone or in pairs. These survivors work to keep each other updated on the witches' movements, but they have recently begun coordinating their efforts for a strike against one of the less organized covens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T09:49:34-08:00","id":1006243,"title":"","content":"So I don't know Demon...at all. So I'll be jumping right to the fan-games for now. So, Seattle!<br /> <br /> <b>Seattle: The Northwest Problem</b><br /> <br /> Seattle is a major gathering point for some kind of massive group of mad scientists, and the local hunter community has steadily been overrun by the bastards since the 1960s. Trying to organize as best as possible in such circumstances, Seattle's hunter community is organized among the principle that the city itself is a lost cause with only a few small holdouts left inside. The area surrounding Seattle however is slightly more their speed, with suburbs and the greater SeaTac area their base to strike at the city in the hopes of reclaiming it.<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey: Inquisitive:</b> Not many members of the Abe have had contact with mad geniuses, and while not as &quot;mystic&quot; as a witch they do offer the same kinds of transformation abilities and even mind control. To even the most jaded sybarite, this is a rich opportunity to get their hands of a pet mad scientist like the nobility of the late Middle Ages and Renaissance.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru: Striking:</b> Geniuses have the ability to make what at first seem like relics, but are in fact something far more strange. Theories on how they do this aside, the AKD typically go out of thir way to destroy any trace of these strange objects due to their unpredictable and dangerous actions if handled by anyone by a mad genius.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones: Negotiating:</b> The Cult of the Phoenix has been trying for three good years to finally open the city enough for the hunters to move in, trying to work out a cease-fire between a group of geniuses who believe that they are a danger to society, and a group of geniuses who think they have a divine right to <i>rule</i> society. Unfortunately, both are quite literally filled with individuals who suffer from whole DSM fulls of psychological illnesses, and negotiations are slow going at the best of times.<br /> <br /> <b>Barrett Commission: Overwhelmed:</b> The &quot;technologies&quot; used by the mad scientists to control people's minds are in a way worse than a vampire's mind control. At least with a vampire, you can stake the problem and easily cover the evidence up with a good shop-vac. Worse, these mad scientists have a way to ghoul people, but in a different way than vampires that makes it almost impossible to tell if they're a slave or not. The Commission so far is playing hell trying to make a foothold in the city government.<br /> <br /> <b>Division Six: Busy: </b>The fact that these people are somehow breaking apart reality but somehow aren't your typical reality deviants has the Seattle cells of Division Six running about in circles trying to get a handle on what exactly they <i>are</i>. Mr. Jones hasn't explicitly given the operations his blessing, but those who contact him most often claim that he seems to be incredibly fearful about Seattle, leading the cells in the area to go on the offensive and try to find out what these &quot;people&quot; are.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron Group: Contracting Out: </b>SeaTac Health Solutions is in the business of medical research, and the mad scientists want to be taken seriously. SeaTac has had several mad scientists and geniuses contracted out for the past few years, and while the experiments <i>sometimes</i> get out of hand (It turns out that several bigfoot sightings since the 1980s are the result of said contractors) STHS has claimed massive advancements in thaumatech implants.<br /> <br /> <b>Long Night: Evangelizing: </b>The Long Night have been on a push to turn much of the area into another region under their control. The major pushers are primarily under the aegis of the Faithful philosophy, seeing the fighting in Seattle as a chance to push closer to their ultimate goal. It doesn't help that many of the pseudo-science theories pushed by the geniuses can be fought on the same level as the more ignorant members of the Long Night moving into the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule: Active: </b>The Loyalists have a history with mad geniuses, and none of it is exactly &quot;rosy&quot;. Many made scientists worked with the Nazis, and to the Loyalists they are an enemy to by absolutely purged at all costs. Unfortunately, the nature of Seattle's situation means that the Loyalists are for now focusing on ingraining themselves within the local hunter community, to gain access to cells that could be useful in finding and eliminating their old foes.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum: Talking:</b> As is the case, people presume that the Catholic Church are vehemently anti-science. That isn't the case as Abbott Mendel would point out, but the Malleus does have a problem with mad scientists running around harming people. Still, several seem to merely be mentally ill, and the Inquisition has been carefully trying to reach out and make entreaties with these geniuses to try and make a common ground in the area. Curiously, the Church has had more success reaching these men and women than the Ascending Ones, the geniuses claiming they're &quot;All too familiar&quot; in their history.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero: Frustrated: </b>With special effects having advanced to the point where anyone can learn how to make digital effects with the right purchases and time, never mind how good you can make practical effects on a cheap budget, most of the videos out of Seattle are treated as &quot;publicity&quot;. This has turned Seattle's Network Zero into unintentional pariahs within their own compact, as every shred of evidence they trot out to the public gets brushed off as a hoax, and gives the geniuses more reason to hate them to &quot;mocking their work&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis: Active:</b> In a strange twist, in Seattle Null Mysteriis is out in force. The mad scientists and geniuses may once have held doctorates and licenses, but the vast majority are dangerous quacks operating on, at best, fringe sciences. Each day reports are published on actions taken by the mad geniuses, and each night the members of ORAS will find these geniuses and not only destroy their work, but scientifically pick apart every reason why they got it wrong to essentially emotionally gutshot the mad scientist. This has made ORAS one of the most valuable groups in Seattle at the present time.<br /> <br /> <b>Talbot Group: Studying:</b> While ORAS handles the breakdown, the Talbot center in the SeaTac area handles the geniuses who want to try and fix themselves. Being able to admit they're mentally unwell and in need of help, the Talbot center is currently treating three of the mad geniuses and two dozen of their &quot;beholden&quot;. Giving them the best advice they can to survive without making horrible creations and giving them small tricks to try and curb their impulses, the Talbot center is working closely with ORAS to make a kind of psychological breakthrough on the topic.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE: Watchful:</b> While many have leveled claims of being corrupted at TFV for their bizarre actions towards vampires, it's nothing compared to the reaction they have when a mad genius is sighted. With a city full of them, TFV patrols the city nightly, keeping an eye on the actions of both the local hunters <i>and</i> the geniuses. Many claim that this is because TFV has found the mad scientists to be a mixed blessing in the past, and so do their best to keep a firm but steady hand over them to remind them of what <i>real</i> future technologies can do to anyone out of line.<br /> <br /> <b>Union: Fighting:</b> In typical fashion, the mad scientists don't think the local villagers are important enough to interact with. Meaning that the local villagers inevitably grab pitchforks and torches. In Seattle, the Union is doing their level best to fight back against the mad geniuses, for fear that their ideas on automation and robotics might kill even <i>more</i> jobs across the country. Unfortunately, the nature of the Vigil in Seattle means that even with the internet, Union cells are hemmed in to their own neighborhoods trying desperately to stay alive.<br /> <br /> <b>Utopia Now: Hiring: </b>While STHS is contracting, Utopia Now is outright hiring geniuses to work on their plan. Since arcologies are at best theoretical technologies, the cells in Seattle have realized that what better way to gain their goal than by simply hiring people who can create what they need, no demon hunting necessary. This doesn't mesh with William Horn's original plan however, and several cells in California and Silicon Valley are becoming rather confrontational with the Seattle cells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 11-23-2016, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T11:38:03-08:00","id":1006310,"title":"","content":"I may add Demon and the reactions of hunters toward them, if you like. Also, may I add some entries about fanmade hunter orgs? (that is, mine and perhaps Skin and Bones's)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T12:59:10-08:00","id":1006348,"title":"","content":"Your own by all rights yeah, and definitely alright with you handling Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:31:25-08:00","id":1006369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1006310#post1006310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(that is, mine and perhaps Skin and Bones's)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a name I haven't heard in a while. A lot of good ideas in that, but marred by a very narrow view of what Hunters should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T14:53:28-08:00","id":1006410,"title":"","content":"You think so? In what way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T02:59:26-08:00","id":1006638,"title":"","content":"I think it had something to do with some ideas being cliche while others were not fully fleshed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T10:39:40-08:00","id":1006766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1006369#post1006369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a name I haven't heard in a while. A lot of good ideas in that, but marred by a very narrow view of what Hunters should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know- I kinda liked it. Sure, some thing require a bit of updating and revising, but the base itself is good, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T11:35:51-08:00","id":1006787,"title":"","content":"Tell me about it. I got Nine Star's permission to redo Society d'Hades - I converted the Aves Manerva into the Athenic Church too but he'd vanished from the internet by the time I went to ask about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T11:58:18-08:00","id":1006796,"title":"","content":"Well Kings, if you want to post for those compacts in the cities I'd love to see what you have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T12:22:25-08:00","id":1006803,"title":"","content":"well, I think I'll start with my own groups' writeup, and then give full attention to Seattle's Demon angle.<br /> <br /> <b><u>New Orleans:</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Cage of Shadows: Underground-</b> while the heresy of the Night Mother was never welcomed among both the living and the dead, the cult is especially despised in the city. Having no more then a few cells, they draw most of their members from among the Jewish population of the city, and they use the already high crime rate in order to hide their practices from both vampires and the hunters who may target them. While they hide, they make sure to keep an open eye and check vampire activities, going out of the shadows only when they recognize the influence of one of the Lilim over the local vampires. In fact, the only reason the cult has managed to survive that long was due to the local leeches recognizing their usefulness and getting rid of the owl-demons, and the cult is well aware of it, making sure to keep their shrines to Lilith hidden and attack vampires only when they can make sure they could make other hunters to take the blame.<br /> <br /> <b>Scharlach Spinnwebe: Supplying-</b> where other hunters find themselves cornered by the bloodsuckers' influence, the Bloody Guild seem to prosper. Worming their way into the city by building a strong network among criminals and corrupted politicians, those hunters has managed to establish a powerful reputation among the leeches. Their blood dolls network has became a useful infrastructure in the eyes of a descent number of bloodsuckers, eliminating competition and creating a ordered feeding ground for any vampire in the city. They integrated so well, in fact, that even without their brainwashing blood magics they have enough allies among the vampires to protect them from potential threats in the All Night Society (not that it didn't helped them to do so). Lately, there have even been some discussion at allowing an &quot;emissary&quot; from the Guild to join the Prince's court. However, all that cooperation with the bloodsuckers has made them to be seen as betrayers and corrupted in the eyes of the local hunters, making them a descent number of enemies in the side of the Vigil.<br /> <br /> <b>Ebony Fangs: Unyielding-</b> little hunters has lost as much as the Fangs during the years, and they do not plan on losing any more than they already did. Ever since the fall of the European Branch, the main power base of the Fangs was in the city, where the Gatekeepers themselves sit and navigate the conspiracy's course in an attempt to survive the changing eras. With so many homicides and crimes being preformed in the city, a fair number of both ghosts and potential recruits are easily found (and that even without including Katrina's influence), giving the conspiracy a bit more room to breath then in almost any other place in the US. In fact, unlike in most places, the Fangs are even able to allow themselves to deal with monsters other than ghosts, attacking leeches and other forms of living dead. Their main target are those vampires who practice a perverted version of Voodoo, twisting the dead and binding them to their own will. Considering that this includes one of the more powerful vampires in the city called the Baron, countless attacks has been preformed against the conspiracy through the years- yet all has failed. The Laws of Irkalla stand strong, protecting their power bases against their enemies- and nothing sort of betrayal would make them fall.<br /> <br /> <b>Followers of Set: Spiraling Down-</b> with so much chaos, violence and blood in the city, it is a little wonder that New Orleans has captured the attention of the vampiric cult known as the Followers of Set. The Cradle of Chaos almost worship the city itself, seeing it as a bloody incarnation of their god. As part of a late trend in the cult, the practice of operating a human faction of hunters in order to protect both the living and the dead from terrible monsters from beyond the veil has started to grow in the city, and the mortal Followers of Set has prospered as one of the few hunter groups which are not under the constant threat of getting killed by the leeches. However, the very structure of the organization makes them too easy to be manipulated, and the high concentration of vampires also means more backstabbing and manipulations among the vampires itself. That has made many of the Sethite leeches to see those hunters as less of a shield and more as a secret weapon to be abused, turning them into assassins meant to hunt down rival vampires and other threats to the cult. More than once those manipulations has even turned one hunter against the other, as members of the Cradle has started to fight among themselves. Seeing as the circumstances practically tear both organisations apart, some among the hunters start to wonder if perhaps they should change the &quot;conditions of their employment&quot; in order to focus on the things which really matter, like dealing with the sudden awakening of sleeping gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T00:35:54-08:00","id":1007081,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Denver:</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Nibiru: Damage Control-</b> For the members of Marduk's Star, Denver is an example for what would happen if they fail their job. With their presence too weak in the area before the coming of the Old God, they were too slow to act against the monstrosity- which cause the deaths of many innocents until it was defeated by the hands of werewolves. Out of feeling responsibility to the situation, the conspiracy has since tripled its presence in the region in order to deal with the legacy of the idigam and destroy or bind the corrupted spirits and monsters it left behind. Some wonder, however, if it shouldn't be better to leave those scraps to the werewolves of Denver and focus their efforts around the newly come Moon Banished.<br /> <br /> <b>E.V.E Institution: Harvesting-</b> the high concentration of werewolves has since made the city into a point of interest to the scientists of E.V.E. With so many lycanthropes which could be used to make the precious Moon Serum- not to mention the large population of Spiders- ignoring Denver would be a missed opportunity- on the other hand, so many werewolves also mean as much as many ways to be killed, which means that if E.V.E wish to survive in the region, it must be careful. As a result, E.V.E does not maintain a constant presence in Denver- sending a single group of Test Subjects to capture as many werewolves and spiders as possible and return to base. While it is dangerous, the so called &quot;empty wolves&quot; of the place do present few interesting possibilities- their essence is much more mutable after being defiled by the mad god, allowing so many new possibilities to evolve. Plus, it allows Test Subjects to use their powers a lot more freely, knowing that the werewolves would probably think that they are just one more experiment of the fallen idigam.<br /> <br /> <b>Church of the Blood Moon: Isolated-</b> the Wold Shepherds do not want to be in Denver. They can trust no one in the city, and their songs may draw more werewolves than they can handle with. Still, the Archbishop of Night feel they must at least try to protect the innocents from the taint of the Wolf Devil, and so he makes sure the conspiracy would have at least a single cell in the wilderness of the Rookies at any given time. Many in the conspiracy think on serving in Denver as a form of punishment for those who break the conspiracy's rules, and those who survive rarely wish to speak about their experiences. They rarely make contact with any other hunter group, other than a casual meeting with he Bear Lodge. In the city of wolves, you can never trust a sheep, after all. <br /> <br /> <b>Aki Ten: Investigating-</b> only after the rise and fall of the idigam did the Aki Ten started to show interest in Denver. The rumors about mad gods, corrupted spirits and all other kinds of horrors crossed the sea, drawing the attention of the New Way. Their main goal is to understand what exactly happened in Denver, what truly was the spirit-monster which twisted the spirit wilds and how can they make sure it would not happen in Japan. Some of their members, however, has different goals in mind- they come to the region to bind the corrupted spirits to their service, exploiting their powers for personal gain. While using a tainted spirit as a shikigami is seen as a taboo, for it is said to corrupt the hunter's soul, it doesn't stop few of the less conventional members from doing so. Worse, some among the leaders of the conspiracy don't wish to research the legacy of the Moon Banished in order to defend themselves from it- but in order to find a way to bind one as their own shikigami, granting them god-like power. Good luck with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T06:20:16-08:00","id":1007200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1006796#post1006796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Kings, if you want to post for those compacts in the cities I'd love to see what you have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Society d'Hades only exist in Paris, France. As for the Athenic Church (do you remember them from the half finished Cults book we worked on?) - I think it's easer to apply your knowledge of America to the Athenic Church than my knowledge of the Athenic Church to America.<br /> <br /> Plus. I don't have the time at the moment. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Links are in my sig index, as always.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T10:34:48-08:00","id":1007315,"title":"","content":"On to San Francisco!<br /> <br /> <b>San Francisco: A Royal Pain</b><br /> <br /> A city like San Francisco is bound to have its odd characters (Hello, Emperor Norton I), but for hunters in the region the problem isn't so much limited to those creatures that would harm humanity. The self-titled &quot;princesses&quot; claim to serve a higher calling to heal and save mankind, but all a good portion of the hunters see is groups of young girls, and even teenagers, running around blasting weird things with magic beams and yammering on and <i>on</i> about friendship being magic. Still, they're doing good, and San Francisco hunters are becoming split on the best way to handle the girls before things reach a boiling point between the two hunter philosophies on the princesses.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru: Magpies: </b>The relics found near a princess are valuable enough that the Spear and Shield seek them out as fast as possible when reported. Massive amounts of power with relatively few or less painful drawbacks compared with witch relics or fae creations make a princess' accessories prized items among high ranking AKD members.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones: Cooperating: </b>Like the princesses, the Cult of the Phoenix would rather see peaceable actions taken rather than outright violence. Working with a group of &quot;ambassadors&quot;, the Ascending Ones have brokered several agreements between hunters and princesses that are considered fair enough to keep in place for a few years now, with the hope that such agreements could one day be permanent.<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey: Angry: </b>Princesses hate the Abbey, and the feeling is mutual. To the Abe, the princesses are the ultimate killjoys in their willingness to try and work with monsters and moral hunters. Several incidents between the Abe and various princesses have led to open conflict, with Abe members killing princesses where they can be found. This has in turn left the Abe with fewer friends than usual, since more than a few other compacts consider the princesses at least less dangerous, and even allies.<br /> <br /> <b>Barrett Commission: Investigating: </b>Princess implies a royal title, and to the Commission another government trying to operate in the United States is suspicious to say the least. Securing the city and county for themselves, the Commission are working to find out more about this &quot;kingdom&quot; that they've heard about.Hopefully it's just a kind of organizing principle rather than an actual government, because if it isn't then the Commission will have to confront what they see as a potential group of assets.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron Group: Investing: </b>Local Cheiron affiliate Redwood Health Supplements and Nutrition has been looking into the princesses for years, and are apparently interested in the idea of bringing some of them into their confidence. Even more surprising, a number of princesses have accepted, to the shock of several cells who have dealt with Redwood before.<br /> <br /> <b>Division Six: Pushing: </b>Where Seattle seems to actively frighten Division Six, San Francisco presents what seems like opportunity. Division Six has three cells in the area, and all have been rumored to be meeting with several more militant hunter cells in the area in order to start tearing down the power structure of the princesses in the city. While these negotiations have allegedly been successes, several other hunters have noted that Division Six only ever seems to strike princesses that typically aren't considered even remotely involved in the day to day fighting in the city.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunt Club: Pining: </b>After the heady days of the 1960s and 70s, the Hunt Club has started to languish recently. Their best members quieted by age or arrest, the club know that they're running out of recruits thanks to how &quot;happy&quot; the princesses are trying to make things. They have a trick or two still up their sleeves though, and hopefully they can bring back their best times sooner than the princesses can realize.<br /> <br /> <b>Illuminated Brotherhood: Fascinated: </b>Compared to many US cities, San Francisco have a relatively benign spiritual landscape. Of course there are always going to be negative and dangerous spirits, but in a city filled with princesses there are an abundance of spirits of joy, hope, and community building a vastly different spiritual landscape than what many in the Brotherhood are used to. This has led them to wonder if princesses might be able to directly affect the spiritual world with their guidance on how to do it.<br /> <br /> <b>Keepers of the Source: Partners: </b>As concerned environmentalists as well as dedicated hunters, the Keepers have come to respect and work alongside princesses, and are one of the largest compacts to push for a peace between the two groups. Keepers cells and princess &quot;nakama&quot; have become a dangerous force in the city, as the Keepers will lobby politically while the princesses use the distraction to root out the darkness in the city.<br /> <br /> <b>Long Night: Conflicted: </b>On one hand, they're clearly doing good. On the other, they clearly aren't using the gifts of God. To the Long Night cells, they have had to wrestle with themselves over whether or not to join in the group of cells that want to see the princesses teaming up with the hunters, and standing apart and becoming regional pariahs.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule: Scouring: </b>The name &quot;Alhambra&quot; keeps popping up in writings related to the princesses, and the Loyalists are wondering if maybe it didn't inspire the name of the palace complex in Granada, Spain. More importantly, it has several similarities to the lost continents of Atlantis, Lemuria, Thule, and Mu, leading the Indebted to wonder if it might not be a physical location they can find. So the Loyalists are on a massive sweep for any and all information regarding the lost city.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge: Confused: </b>So wrapped up in trying to save monsters from themselves if they can, the Lucifuge are at a loss to explain princesses in their worldview. Beings so wrapped in love and compassion aren't the kind of foe the Lucifuge are used to, and several times a Lucifuge member in California has had to quickly explain to a princess that they're fighting the same enemies before they get their asses kicked.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum: Set Against: </b>The Malleus had a time dealing with the princesses in Scotland, and has since spread the word that they're no friend to the Church or their flock. The Malleus are doing their best to spread the word in San Francisco about the princesses, how they literally steal hope or create dangerous cults just as much as acting like they're saving the world. A few unaffiliated cells have listened, though the larger hunter community feels that the Malleus are letting past actions judge present events.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero: Ecstatic: </b>Princesses have their ideas on secrecy, but Network Zero in the city has earned their trust to the point where they feel perfectly safe and willing to work with the compact by willingly showing off their abilities and taking NetZo cells with them on their fights against what they call &quot;The Darkness&quot;. This has turned Network Zero into the city's leading experts on the princesses, their goals, and who they're fighting.Which has made many NetZos giddy with excitement.<br /> <br /> <b>Night Watch: Peaceable: </b>On the West Coast, the Night Watch prefers a more community-focused touch compared to the violence in the Midwest and on the East Coast. Respecting this stance by the Watch, several princesses have actually become honorary members, walking the same patrols and riding the same subways as the Watch patrols. Many hunters warn that this is getting too close for comfort, but the Watch are more than willing to accept the help that other hunters have typically denied them.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis: Planning: </b>Since the princesses seem so willing to work with hunters against the strange and unknown, Null Mysteriis in San Francisco is in the early stages of setting up a series of tests to see if the magic of a princess can't actually be the first paranormal phenomenon that can be truly quantified and measured.<br /> <br /> <b>Talbot Group: Thankful: </b>Princesses are much more mindful of psychological pain than most hunters even care to acknowledge, and their work will often involve getting help for those left behind after a raid or street fight. Several princesses have volunteered to work with the Talbot Group in San Francisco, helping the group find a place for wolf-blooded, recovering ghouls, and sensitives learning about their abilities along with the more mundane but no less important cases of mental illness and counseling.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE: Hunting: </b>Where the Commission is trying to piece things together, TFV isn't waiting around to find out. Mentions of a &quot;kingdom&quot; are officially considered a threat to the functioning government, and MRUs in northern California have been ordered to eliminate princesses wherever they're found, interrogation is only an option when they can be taken alive and by surprise.<br /> <br /> <b>Union: Wary: </b>As a majority of San Francisco seems to fawn over the princesses, the Union in the city wants little to do with them. Of course they'll accept help if they need it, but they aren't so willing to throw open the doors for the princesses the way other groups are. This has led to a partnership of sorts between the Union and Malleus, both carefully watching the princesses for fear of what they might do if too many hunters let their guard down.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU: Searching:</b> More than a few serial killers and kidnappers have operated in the San Francisco area, and VASCU is worried that there are still more roaming the region that they haven't found. Though the search for the Zodiac is just about a lost cause at this point, the reality is that there are still several unsolved serial murder cases that the unit believes should be considered high priority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 11-25-2016, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T13:08:19-08:00","id":1007818,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Boston</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Museum Secretorum: Fascinated-</b> so many witches gathering in one place also means so many beautiful wonders to add to their collection. One of the conspiracy's largest museums is found in the city, and it is well guarded by the members of the group to make sure no witch would be foolish enough to try and steal their precious collections. Many new potential recruits could be found among the many students of the city's colleges and universities, and the Museum usually send &quot;talent hunters&quot; to lure such students to their path. As whole, the Museum prefers to avoid actually hunting witches to their collection in the city, knowing that one wrong move and they'll bring the whole willworking population upon their heads, and as such most of their time is invested at getting interviews from mages and other supernatural beings and collect some rare items. Unknown to most of the witches, however, one of their factions (called the Mysterium) has made a certain alliance with the hunters- the Museum would let them access their archives and investigate some of their rarer phenomena, and in exchange certain renegade witches (called &quot;Left Handed&quot;) would be sent to their collection as their &quot;punishment&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Order of the Void: Getting Armed-</b> the followers of the Nameless has a long term goal, and they believe that Boston may be one of the finale moves in their grand game over the Void. The Inner Council has lately announced the beginning of Phase Two, and Boston seems to going to take a major part in that plan to achieve the blueprints of the Abyss. While it is all very hush-hush, all the hunters know that a war is coming, and that they should supply and gather their resources toward the coming battle. Their target- a local cult named simple as the &quot;Red Word&quot;. While the Order has never liked those witches who communicate with the Void (especially after the events of the Burned Over District), and their cannibalistic rituals are more then enough to make every member of the conspiracy to want to put a bullet in their heads, the Inner Council seem to have their own plans- something about time travel, or alternative histories. While the war would be bloody, thankfully most of the witches seem to hate such cults as much as the Order does. They might even help them- as long as they won't discover that the Order is a cult all by itself.<br /> <br /> <b>A.S.T.R.A.L: Threat Detection-</b> why so many mages seem to gather around the region? What is so special about the city to make witches search for it? A.S.T.R.A.L don't know, but they are bent to find out. All their data resources seem to show that Boston has some importance to the mages, and that means they have to find the source and burn it clean. Until then, the book burners have a strategy to deal with the threats of the city- they donate the to local colleges in order to get a foothold over information, targeting both potential members who seem to relate to their ideology and students who start to show signs of starting to Awake, giving them enough time to monitor the potential threats and devour the Awakening before it even takes place. Some other members, however, seem to relate to the more &quot;traditional&quot; strategy of their company- they break into the houses of witches, devour their grimoires and relics and drain every Source they can find. Some even preach to the locals about hidden dangers, taking the roles of priests or just traditionalists who fear the change in the city's nature. Sure, exploiting racism and harming innocents is wrong- but the dangers of uncontrolled knowledge are far worse.<br /> <br /> <b>Nemontemi: Driven-</b> while the group's headquarters is found mostly in Latin America, with the rise of Hispanic population that strain of cursed blood has found its way through the US- and Boston became the focus of their attention. The star gods of the void are drawn to the acts of willworkers, after all, and a city with such an high population of mages means that the chances for such an event to happen is just are just as high. Few local cells of the Star Children operate in the city, ignoring most of the internal politics of the witches and focusing their attention around those magicians who speak with the Abyss and summon its denizens as servants, although the local soul thieves also seem to be draw their attention, as their broken soul is tainted by the same darkness of the Beyond. The most disturbing reports are about the cult of the Red Word- their cannibalistic behavior and the rumors about their faith in a world which is yet to come once the previous would end are just too similar to the old rituals of their peoples for them to ignore. Perhaps they are another group of people manipulated by dark gods. Perhaps this time, they are right. And maybe, just maybe some of their own support the cult from the shadows. Whatever the case, the have to check it out- and destroy the cult if needed to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T00:28:43-08:00","id":1007977,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Detroit</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Ashen Collective: Scavenging-</b> there is nothing the Alchemist of the Grey like then plundering a dead corpse. They gathering of the Reanimated has drawn their attention, and the general decline of the city made them very interested in experimenting on what would happen to a place which its rot is accelerated by the gathering of the living dead. Many believe it is only a matter of time until a major Firestorm would swap the city, devouring the rot and giving new life- and they plan on capturing its flames as it would happen. Others are just as happy at taking over old assets and make them into traps meant to capture the Reanimated to their researches. Even regular corpses aren't safe from their touch, and they are willing to pay a lot for a steady supply of test subjects- no matter how and why they died.<br /> <br /> <b>Custodes Ignis: Sort Handed-</b> the Fire Guards saw the fall of many empires through the years, and they know the signs. Detroit is only a symptom, not the disease- but the problem should be dealt with before it is too late. Many of them would have been happy to blame the Reanimated for the rot, but they know that while the supernatural explanation could be comforting, as in giving them something to do, sometimes there is something they can do. They still deploy their cells at an attempt to cleanse at least some of the effect created by the prometheans, relieving the supernatural influences of the Disquiet and the Wasteland over the city- yet the root of the problem is deeper than that. There is little they can do with mundane fall of an empire, no matter how much they try. Perhaps it is time to find a new empire to serve- China could be a good candidate, perhaps.<br /> <br /> <b>Sabaoth: Crusading-</b> while the Burning Serpents serve as mercenaries, they never forget their true calling- that is, to clean the world from the taint of stolen fire. The reanimated who come to a city to which they don't belong, and souls touched by them sense the fear and turn upon each other. The general atmosphere of distrust allows easy recruiting to the group which gives them someone else to blame- someone to hate, to despise and fear. The reanimated are the reason Detroit is failing, they say, and you should fight against those who don't belong to this world. The truth of the matter is not a concern- all that matters is that it is &quot;you&quot; against &quot;them&quot;, and that you should join the angels in their crusade against the walking dead.<br /> <br /> <b>Ebony Fangs: Cautious-</b> the emissaries of the underworld has always found themselves growing where others rot. Detroit is dying, and while it does its ghosts are left behind- restless shades of the past clinging to life. Knowing that a fall of such a city without a careful management could be a disastrous event, few cells of the Fangs has already started a some sort of &quot;funeral&quot; to the city. Unlike in the more rich regions of the US, the fall of Detroit also means higher chances to recruit, bolstering their numbers enough to be able to maintain a constant, worthy to note presence in the city. The reanimated in general has captured the interest of the group- as being neither truly dead or alive, the Laws of Irkalla seem to operate funny near them, treating them as either (or both or none) of the states. With their population being so rare, the Fangs see Detroit as an excellent chance to study those beings and retrieve at least some of the information lost in the European Branch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T00:29:03-08:00","id":1008446,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Miami</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Orchestra Fatalibus: In Plain Sight-</b> while the Singers' true power base is found back in Europe, Miami is their largest center in the US. Drawn together with the many musicians, dancers and other performers, the conspiracy has established a strong network of information sharing among each other, and even adapted some of its ages old songs (both magical and communicative) into fresh new styles- rumba, techno, hip hop and even rap all have their own fans, and it is their duty to give the people the music they wish for.. especially if more people listening to their songs means more people influenced by them. By using the influenced masses as both as part of their information network and in order to uncover hidden fairies, the Orchestra is able to confuse, misdirect and befuddle their enemies, sending them toward secondary threats while the true power lies hidden.<br /> <br /> <b>Garden of Hesperides: Involved-</b> unlike some other hunter groups, the Herbalists did not came to Miami in order to hunt the Fairies- they came to help them. They walk inside the thorny Hedge in order to find new lost souls and direct them to the great Courts in order to help them adapt to their new situation. They also use their skills and Silver Roads in order to harvest and supply rare Goblin Fruits to the changelings, and they hold a number of pacts and pledges with the local Courts for mutual help and alliance. Considering the large amount of time they spend in the Hedge, those hunters always keep an open eye in a case they'll hear rumors about a coming Huntsman, sending a word of warning in advance and give the changelings some time to prepare- and in worst case scenario, their Silver Roads may offer a temporary escape from the Wild Hunt.. as long as you don't stray from the path, that is.<br /> <br /> <b>Chasseurs de Tetes: Zealot-</b> the Headhunters seem to hate Miami with burning passion. A land so well controlled by nobles and fate is the antithesis for all they work for. The Idea seem to rage against the city, summoning hunters from across the sea to come and fight until their last breath in the name of freedom. Such sudden outbursts of the Enraged come and die out every some time, as they raid local power bases of the fairies and cut off their heads or die trying. Meanwhile, the changelings have since managed to understand that those attacks seem to be connected to each other, but they don't seem to manage to piece a full picture of their enemy. Their magics seem to fail around them, and the Wyrd itself is cut by their hands. They blame them for a group manipulated by some Huntsman or even a Gentry, and search the Hedge for further information about who those &quot;Headhunters&quot; may be. Ironically, the Headhunters don't hunt only the changelings in the city- Florida had its fair share of serial killers, and the Chesseurs are not above tracking new potential recruits and convert them to the Idea, or cut off the heads of those who can't rise above their murderous nature. After all, its not like they are using them anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T15:39:20-08:00","id":1008699,"title":"","content":"And we're on to San Diego/Tijuana!<br /> <br /> <b>San Diego/Tijuana: A Fishing We Will Go</b><br /> <br /> As the Vigil is a worldwide duty, so to is it international in San Diego and Tijuana. Even with a border bisecting the metro area, the hunters in the region have created an entire cottage industry centered around getting cells through to both cities to carry on the Vigil in spite of the US and Mexican authorities. The bigger problem is the reality that the region is being overrun by a race of fish-men who are intent on being worshiped as gods by any human under their controlling presence. The monsters don't even need to make an effort to control the minds of men, their simple existence is enough to twist a man's mind to abject worship.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones: At War:</b> There is no other way to describe it. The Cult of the Phoenix is fighting a war in Tijuana. A fish-woman by the name of Tia Ramona has been working to dismantle their operations in the local drug trade, and she and her followers have succeeded in taking down many of the conspiracy's more prominent members. While the local Ascending Ones are fighting back to protect their holdings from what seems to be a dispute over territory, some suspect that the Leviathan's campaign is being carried out for more personal reasons. But their drug connections have come in handy for getting people across the border, and it's enabled the Ascending Ones to call in favors they aren't shy about using.<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey: Chartering:</b> In the minds of the Abbey membership, San Diego is practically akin to a fishing vacation. Setting their clubhouse out on the coast as close to the border as possible, the Abbey will charter to sail as close to Mexican waters and go against any fish-men they can find. That several international incidents have nearly occurred thanks to the recklessness of the Abe doesn't seem to matter.<br /> <br /> <b>Barrett Commission:</b><b> Networking:</b> With the threat of the fish-men so pervasive, the Commission knows that securing San Diego and putting the people who can save Tijuana in power will be next to impossible. The Commission is trying to create a system of hunters to use as proxies, directing them to the threats that are the most obvious to both sides in order to break the monster power base in city government and make a buffer to the south.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron Group: Fishing: </b>The &quot;leviathans&quot; are complete gold-mines for the company, and their office in San Diego is constantly sponsoring &quot;biological expeditions&quot; off the shores of both countries to steal the most choice pieces. There's also rumors of some kind of &quot;rift&quot; where even more amazing samples and specimens can be found, and that the leviathans know <i>exactly</i> how to reach it.<br /> <br /> <b>Faithful of Shulpae: Growing:<br /> <br /> Long Night: Warring:</b> &quot;Though Shalt Have No Other Gods Before Me&quot;. The Long Night are often peaceful, but a direct affront to their God like the fish-men will most certainly <i>not</i> stand. The Long Night has been waging a hard conflict against the fish-men and their cults, doing their best to try and draw the poor deluded fools away from their false idols and back to the loving arms of a merciful deity.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule:</b> <b>Fleeing:</b> The Loyalists believe that even if one of the cities can be cleared, the other will still remain a fetid hole of monsters. Orders from Munich are that the Loyalists in the city should grab what they can and get out if they don't want to be abandoned. A few are waiting as long as possible, trying to spread what they safely can to other hunters before the Loyalists leave entirely.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge: Unrestrained: </b>Fighting against evil that is outright evil isn't hard for the Lucifuge. The Seventh Generation have tried before to make some kind of contact with the leviathans, and it ended with <i>fifteen</i> of them dead at once. Such a loss is too much to bear even if their numbers replenish with each death, and the Lady has decided that such creatures are too far gone to save no matter what mercy can be given.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum: Stalwart: </b>The leviathans have been recorded multiple times in the Church's history, from the coasts of the Levant to cults devoted to J\u00f6rmungandr in the north of Europe. Knowing that these threats can destroy whole communities and even small nations, the Malleus have used their power on both sides of the border to at least shore up the defenses, ensuring that the monsters can have no easy time moving between the two nations.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero: War Correspondence:</b> The Secret Frequency has been smuggling and posting footage from the border for a good fifteen years by this point, trying to get the information to other cities that might be wrapped up by the fish-people. Unfortunately the fish-men don't like this, and Network Zero has been forced to fight back. Worse, reports are spreading that the videos are having the complete opposite effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Night Watch: Stymied: </b>Since the fish-men can promise their followers safety and security, it often means that local leeches are a prime target for their cults. This has left the Night Watch in a bind, since their more public efforts to protect their communities are focused more on mortal criminals than the paranormal. While this has given the Watch a more favorable reputation in San Diego than in other US cities, it has left the leadership wondering how much good they can do for their fellow hunters.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis: Floundering: </b>Though some of the group think that maybe the fish-men are some kind of proof of the &quot;aquatic ape&quot; theory, most are more focused on the reality that these things are problems. Dissections of corpses reveal multiple atavistic growths in each one, whether it be gills, scales, or even proof of hermaphroditic reproductive capabilities. None of it has helped ORAS develop anything more concrete however, and the fish-men are sending their cultists after them to keep their secrets safe. <br /> <br /> <b>Talbot Group: Overwhelmed: </b>You would think that the cults are bad enough, but deprogramming a fish-man's followers is only part of the problem. It turns out that some individuals suffer an opposite effect, an intense hatred that leaves them consumed with a self-destructive mission to kill all the fish-men they find. For now describing them as &quot;Ahabs&quot;, the Talbot center in San Diego is facing more cases of both brainwashed cultists and rage-driven Ahabs.<br /> <br /> <b>Union: Battered: </b>Left adrift on both sides of the border, the working stiffs of both cities have been overrun by fish-cults, lunatics driven to kill fish-men wherever they're found, and the conspiracies leaving them to dry. Still the Union continually builds up, grabbing families left in ruins by the fish-cults and forming cells practically every week. Casualties are high on both sides of the border, but a major Union push in Tijuana might be the key to secure at least the Southern border.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE: Building: </b>As a major military city, TFV has had to contend with the fish-men in San Diego for some time. For years it was a running tit-for-tat fight, but recently command has decided that they've had enough. Intelligence has been found that places at least one subversive leviathan element within Marine Corps Recruit Depot San Diego, and that's one too many. TFV is building up a strike force, with several MRUs seconded to the mission. Soon, they've sweep the city, and into Tijuana if necessary, to clear it out.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU: Forgotten: </b>With all the major players in San Diego focused on the fish-men and vice versa, VASCU has been tracking several individuals they don't realize are Ahabs. The agents have also been subject to constant psychic pressure from the creatures, but have formed their own support system to make sure they can stand through it and fight. Possibly making themselves immune to the creatures, VASCU may one day be the trump card the Vigil needs in San Diego, and possibly even Tijuana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 11-28-2016, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T00:52:30-08:00","id":1008850,"title":"","content":"<b><u>San Diego/Tijuana</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones: At War:</b> There is no other way to describe it. The Cult of the Phoenix is fighting a war in Tijuana. A fish-woman by the name of Tia Ramona has been working to dismantle their operations in the local drug trade, and she and her followers have succeeded in taking down many of the conspiracy's more prominent members. While the local Ascending Ones are fighting back to protect their holdings from what seems to be a dispute over territory, some suspect that the Leviathan's campaign is being carried out for more personal reasons.<br /> <br /> <b>Followers of Set: Hounded:</b> With infighting plaguing their cells in the two cities, the Cradle of Chaos finds itself in a precarious state. Some of the local Leviathans have killed many of their hunters, and enthralled several others in their wake. These thralls not only strike down their former comrades, but have ruthlessly slain many of the conspiracy's allies among the local Kindred. In response, the Followers of Set attempt to seek out aid from the cities' other supernaturals in the hope of forming a stronger resistance against the Wicked Tribe. This has led to them forging an alliance with the Barrett Commission due to their common goals.<br /> <br /> <b>Habibti Ma: Frantic:</b> If there are places where the compact's efforts have difficulty gaining ground, then San Diego and Tijuana would be counted among them. The fish-men exert a strong grip over their cults, and it is further reinforced by the familial ties they have with many of the members. To make things worse, many among Habibti Ma risk falling under their influence as they spend more time trying to pull people away from the monsters' influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-27-2016, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T07:06:47-08:00","id":1008899,"title":"","content":"<b><u>New Orleans</u> [Skin &amp; Bones]</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Dirge: Wild Card:</b> With a safehouse having been present since Hurricane Katrina, the Dirge is one of the more established compacts in New Orleans. But although they are a nightly thorn to the local vampires, their Vigil has also led them to clash with other hunters in the city. The Cheiron Group and VALKYRIE are particularly at odds with them. Even so, both the Night Watch and the Union typically consider them as allies, and the Lucifuge has used them as catspaws to strike at a few vampires that they cannot hit directly.<br /> <br /> <b>The Wordsmiths: Neutral:</b> While already a small group in New Orleans, the Wordsmiths are at risk of being driven out altogether. Their only clinic in the city is an open secret to both vampires and other hunters, and it has come close to being destroyed from either group many times. However, one of the local vampire elders is an ally and ward of theirs, and a faction among the Long Night's Merciful frequently work with them. These unlikely alliances have made the Wordsmiths a neutral party in the Vigil, allowing them to survive thus far. It is a tenuous arrangement, though. Many among the Night Watch have been looking for any excuse to attack the compact's clinic, and several of the vampire elder's enemies are also keen on purging the Wordsmiths due to their efforts in freeing some of their ghouls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:27:12-08:00","id":1009365,"title":"","content":"Okay, with all the major fan game lines done and with no ideas what cities are left, I had an idea for a Slasher-centric city.<br /> <br /> <b>Cleveland: Fittingly Named</b><br /> <br /> In the US, one city has gained a dubious and dangerous reputation for the people that seem to flock to it. Out of all the cities in the US, the city has an almost magnetic pull to those who kill for killing's sake. Slashers are just as drawn to the city, and the Vigil in Cleveland is focused on trying to make it through another night without a double-digit body county of innocent people being racked up.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron Group: Recruiting:</b> You have to be a special kind of crazy to be part of Field Projects, and most slashers are just the kind of crazy Cheiron is looking for to capture the big money projects. Sure, you lose a few cells to competition, infighting, arrest, but it's a small price to pay when you literally get a baker's dozen of werewolf bodies or staked vampires for research even two weeks. Unfortunately, the scuttlebutt around Cleveland is that some kind of doctor is in the area, and making life hell for Cheiron.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunt Club:</b> <b>Ruling:</b> The city is the Hunt Club's unofficial headquarters at this point, with the ranking members making annual and even bi-annual trips to hone their skills and talk over their scores with their peers. Controlling the city through a mixture of blackmail, extortion, and just inviting the powerful to join them on their romps, the Club have little to fear from the local hunters and even less to fear from those &quot;moralists&quot; at VASCU.<br /> <br /> <b>Long Night:<br /> <br /> Loyalists of Thule, Lucifuge: Seeking: </b>The Loyalists don't think that this many serial killers wind up in Cleveland out of coincidence. There must be an occult reason for why it's happening, and the Loyalists are using their own experience with the murderous to make their own theories. The leading one is that there's a kind of power hidden in the area, one that these murderers and slashers are somehow drawn to. Unbeknownst to the Hunt Club, the Lucifuge have a presence in the region and are seeking them out. The constant murders by the club have attracted the attentions of Milan, and a cell has been sent from New York to try and halt the bloodshed if only for a time. The more pressing matter is, like the Loyalists, trying to puzzle out a reason so many of the murderous are being drawn like moths to a flame in the city.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum:</b><b> Bound:</b> The Malleus in Cleveland are actually hindered by the Church itself in trying to handle the problems involving slashers. Explicit orders have never come from Bauldino or Gallaher on what to do about the city, and the cells are trying to pull themselves together for some kind of plan to fight back against the murderers without being thrown in jail. The only out they can see is using the Cleveland Emerald Society as a recruiting ground for police that might be willing to fight.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero: Dying:</b> In a sick joke out of Wes Craven, the NetZos in Cleveland are dying each night because they're trying to put out the truth. Since slashers are still somewhat human, the Network isn't as bothered by the conspiracies as in other cities, but the slashers more than make up for it since Network Zero keeps trying to stop them by putting their faces and victims up across the internet and in people's faces.<br /> <br /> <b>Night Watch: Strong:</b> In a city like Cleveland, the Night Watch stand as a beacon of hope. Riding public transit with mace and (if they can get the right permits) a pistol, the real heavy hitters on the Watch stay out of the spotlight as best as possible to strike at the slashers where they can be found. For once acting in close concert with the police, the Watch are still stymied whenever they confront a killer who uses their social status to evade the law time and again.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis:</b> <b>Studying:</b> Since their paper on slashers was published, ORAS have become the de facto experts of slashers, and have setup a facility in Cleveland trying to puzzle out whether they can be saved from themselves or just drugged and left to languish in a cell. Two relatively sane (for a very loose use of the word) slashers have been found, one who keeps killing criminals and one that suffered grievous abuse for a major birth defect. With the Talbot Group still far and away in either New York or the West Coast, ORAS psychologists are gently trying to convince the two that not every problem needs to be resolved with outright murder. Suffice to say, it's slow going, and the second slasher is starting to give the staff disconcerting glances when they come in the office.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU: Building:</b> Knowing full-well that the city is under the grip of the slasher cabal known as the Hunt Club, VASCU agents are preparing the mother of all legal smackdowns. Experienced agents have been brought in to help catalogue every piece of evidence and poke holes in every alibi. Wintergreen agents have been put on dozens of stakeouts, tracking and marking each night that a murder has occurred when a suspected member is in the same area. Such an operation might have been put down by the special agent in charge of the office years ago, if Washington wasn't so paranoid about their being compromised that the whole thing is being kept locked tight from them.<br /> <br /> <b>WIP</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 11-28-2016, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T13:38:20-08:00","id":1009920,"title":"","content":"<b><u>New York</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Ebony Fangs: Overflooded-</b> there is not place to show the Fangs' weakness like New York. The big apple is, more or less, the American Dream personified. A nihilistic group such as the Fangs find themselves at odds with the general atmosphere, and many of them ends up as another &quot;crazy homeless guy&quot; on the streets. Add to that the great number of ghosts in the city and the well founded network of ghostwalkers, and it is a wonder the hunters of Irkalla haven't all went crazy already. Many of them fear the city, knowing that once they'll make a single step into its limits the screams of the dead and the visions of horror just won't stop. Those who do live in New York force the Old Laws for protection on daily basis, doing whatever they can in order to silence the dead just to get one night of nightmare-free sleep.<br /> <br /> <b>Pomegranate Deme: Prospering-</b> for the Memory Collectors, New York is a treasure. So many restless souls waiting to be bound into their little boxes, so much knowledge waiting to be recovered and collected to their storage rooms. They maintain dozens of small antique shops which deal with fetters and bound dead bellow the surface, and meet up in graveyards in order to preform their old rites. If not only for all of those nosy &quot;sin eaters&quot;, who spend so much time and stealing their fetters and freeing the bound ghosts, the Collectors would have already taken over the city. Still, the high concentration of Eurydices and Orpheuses has its own benefits- for who knows what hidden secrets of the Bellow hide beneath their masked faces?<br /> <br /> <b>Order of the Nameless: Steady-</b> ever since the days of the Burned Over District, the Order's base of operation was and stayed in New York. Maintaining a number of alliances with the local witches, the Order was more or less accepted as a regular occult society with a wide network among the so called &quot;apostates&quot;. While the Order has learned from its past mistakes and no longer allow witches position of power within the organization, the Inner Council does accept Auditions with the local mages to give them advises about Abyssal incursions and share their knowledge about the worlds beyond. Since the beginning of Phase Two, such meetings has became even more frequent, as the competition over the Black Sun Map force them to use any asset in their disposal.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Syndicate: Filthy Rich-</b> the hunters of the Syndicate proudly claim that no other hunter group is as a &quot;New Yorker&quot; as they are. Growing for the bottom of the streets, their leader's craftiness and their strong alliances with the local spirit world has made them into a power to reckon with. Almost all lower tiers hunters have an account at &quot;Vigil Insurances&quot; or have their accounts and real life businesses managed by the company. While the spiritual ecosystem is, more or less, under their control- the so called &quot;ghost plague&quot; is a problem. Worse, it seems that those people who died once in the past see little to no need in things like &quot;life insurance&quot;. While the world of the dead is an enigma for the Syndicate, like every good company it already has plans of expansion. Donnie has collected few highly renowned grimoires about the Great Bellow and the shades of the dead, and already has plans on how to exploit the city's &quot;natural resources&quot; for his own good. Sure, the Syndicate's hold over mundane and supernatural assets has already made them into filthy, stinking rich- but if New York has taught them something, is that you should never settle for what you have. That's how you get eaten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T00:58:47-08:00","id":1010097,"title":"","content":"<u><b>San Diego/Tijuana</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru: Covetous:</b> While they count the cities' fish-men among their many shapeshifting enemies, the Shield and the Spear is active at San Diego for a different reason. The San Diego Museum of Man has quite a few Relics in its care, and the conspiracy is keen on acquiring them for safekeeping. However, they are hampered by the fact that the museum's curator is a Leviathan himself -- one not keen on having any exhibits vandalized by looters.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Also. I'd suggest Phoenix, Arizona from the Promethean 2e core as another setting to tackle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T10:18:38-08:00","id":1010248,"title":"","content":"I actually don't have any of the 2E books or any information about what's going on in them.<br /> <br /> Which is why I'm moving on to some of the lesser developed fan-games, because I can at least make a reasonable presumption based on them compared to stuff I know nothing about. If anyone else has any cities they think would be good to add, jump on and hit it.<br /> <br /> <b>Las Vegas: The Devils Playground</b><br /> <br /> Sin City isn't just a cute like sobriquet that got slapped on Vegas for the vices that literally keep the city's economy from sinking into the sands. Demons have moved into the city in force, tempting men and women to their darker deals and ideas on how to get ahead. Though hunters have always been present in the city, since the mob left Vegas the Vigil has suddenly faced even harder times against their enemies. It appears that the mob was enough of a tempter for humans without demons getting involved, but with their grip destroyed by the Feds the demons have moved in en masse, knowing that the desperate would flock to them.<br /> <br /> <b>Pittsburgh: Getting Ugly</b><br /> <br /> With so many of the &quot;hunchbacks&quot; in the city, hunters are conflicted on how to treat them. Some believe that the poor bastards should be protected from themselves and their enemies, since no one else seems willing to. Other hunters feel that they're monsters even to other monsters, so better to kill off the disease before it can spread. A third faction of hunters feel that they're being too harsh of the hunchbacks to just kill them, and that their willingness to do anything for a master is exactly the tool the Vigil needs in Pittsburgh. It isn't unusual to have entire &quot;cancer cells&quot; of hunchbacks running nightly on the orders of a compact or conspiracy, or even a well-connected lone cell. This has threatened to turn into an arms race, with hunters preparing to snatch up as many &quot;I-Gors&quot; as possible for their own ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Atlanta: Sickening</b><br /> <br /> Stories coming out of Atlanta are that there's a kind of disease spreading, some kind of literally smart bug that affects people in different ways. The only reason that it hasn't broken out completely is that the Feds are keeping it so tight under wraps that not even Network Zero has much on them. After the panics about Ebola though, no one can really blame them. Fortunately, the Vigil in Atlanta is relatively well organized, considering the massive Federal presence in the city that no one wants to call down on themselves. So each night, cells are trying to figure out just what is the story behind these rumors of a strange dangerous disease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T11:13:28-08:00","id":1010270,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry but what game lines are you referring to here?<br /> <br /> Also, might others add their own settings to this thread? Like crossover cities and other strange things or would that be stepping on your toes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T11:33:01-08:00","id":1010276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1010270#post1010270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry but what game lines are you referring to here?<br /> <br /> Also, might others add their own settings to this thread? Like crossover cities and other strange things or would that be stepping on your toes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure Flyboy is talking about the fanlines. Seattle is Genius the Transgression, San Francisco is Princess: the Hopeful, San Diego/Tijuana is Leviathan: The Temptest, Las Vegas is the Spainish pre-Descent fanline Demon: The Redemption, Pitsburgh is Hunchback: The Lurching, and Atlanta is Pathogen: The Infected.<br /> <br /> Regarding Beast: the Primordial, does anyone have any idea what would be a good hub city for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T14:25:33-08:00","id":1010339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1010276#post1010276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Beast: the Primordial, does anyone have any idea what would be a good hub city for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts immediately go to &quot;Candyman&quot; - a Clive Barker movie which put a living myth against the backdrop of urban decay. I think Beast could do worse than trying to replicate that feel. As far as United States are concerned, Wikipedia ranks St. Louis and Baltimore as most crime-ridden cities. Detroit and New Orleans come in second, but are already taken by Promethean and Vampire, respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T15:23:34-08:00","id":1010365,"title":"","content":"I feel that since Beasts work through fear, and Baltimore is infamous for crime at this point, that's my vote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T17:35:57-08:00","id":1010418,"title":"","content":"I may have already written my own version of it, but I vote Savannah Georgia, which is also infamous for crime lately. The way the locals talk about the 80s/90s gang lord Ricky Jivens, even decades after his conviction, seems very apex beast's myth to me and the fact that Little Ricky's gang was the origin for many urban legends about inner city street gangs only makes it fit more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T22:48:43-08:00","id":1010526,"title":"","content":"Damn man, that's a sweet writeup. Well, what do you guys think for Beast, Baltimore or Savannah?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T11:53:44-08:00","id":1010737,"title":"","content":"Baltimore always needs some love, and I think would be an interesting setting for Beast. Though it involves getting into some dicey territory vis-a-vis Baltimore's complex racial politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:17:50-08:00","id":1010757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1010526#post1010526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn man, that's a sweet writeup. Well, what do you guys think for Beast, Baltimore or Savannah?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, The only regret I have about that write up is not knowing about Jivens when I first wrote the beast section, because I seriously would have made him the former Apex of the Savannah Hive. To this day, Jivens is a source of fear to Savannah, in part due a couple scandals where he was found to have dating site profiles and a Facebook page from inside prison (and thus possibly be giving orders to his men from prison via the internet), and in part because the recent rise in violent crime in Savannah has people worrying that the city might see a successor to Jivens that carries on his murderous legacy<br /> <br /> As for Baltimore and racial politics, Savannah's racial politics are weird, but in a way that might be easier to handle since it has more to do with corruption in the city's various ethnic political machines than with outright racism and discrimination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T14:39:38-08:00","id":1010825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1010757#post1010757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Baltimore and racial politics, Savannah's racial politics are weird, but in a way that might be easier to handle since it has more to do with corruption in the city's various ethnic political machines than with outright racism and discrimination.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean Baltimore has that too. All that and a bag of Utz. It's more a matter of recognizing that you cannot do any sort of Baltimore write up without touching race in some way. Its history is inexorably linked with it, and if one is going to talk about crime there's only so long you can avoid talking about race. One can certainly make every attempt to fastidiously avoid the topic, but that is a conscious omission that pretty much amounts to ignoring an elephant in the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T15:42:05-08:00","id":1010849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1010825#post1010825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean Baltimore has that too. All that and a bag of Utz. It's more a matter of recognizing that you cannot do any sort of Baltimore write up without touching race in some way. Its history is inexorably linked with it, and if one is going to talk about crime there's only so long you can avoid talking about race. One can certainly make every attempt to fastidiously avoid the topic, but that is a conscious omission that pretty much amounts to ignoring an elephant in the room.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Savannah is the same way. I suppose it comes down to the other details about the respective cities. Savannah is rather proud of it's weirdness and spookyness and has a lot of wonderful folklore for hunters to look into, but it is you guys' decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T19:26:41-08:00","id":1010904,"title":"","content":"You've made a good case for Savannah. I just wanted to give one of my adopted cities a plug.<br /> <br /> I don't have any kind of write up for Baltimore (except I think in some old Requiem notes somewhere). I did do a Vigil setting for DC though, which I may drop on here if I can locate the notebook it lives in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 12-01-2016, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T10:55:34-08:00","id":1011137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1010904#post1010904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've made a good case for Savannah. I just wanted to give one of my adopted cities a plug.<br /> <br /> I don't have any kind of write up for Baltimore (except I think in some old Requiem notes somewhere). I did do a Vigil setting for DC though, which I may drop on here if I can locate the notebook it lives in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, Savannah is soon to be my hometown, so I understand the desire to give an adopted hometown a CofD makeover. I'll let you guys finish deciding what city to do and get back to you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T14:25:06-08:00","id":1011222,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm. Savannah for Beast, any hints for Deviant yet? Because maybe that could be Baltimore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T14:46:38-08:00","id":1011228,"title":"","content":"What about Phoenix, Arizona? It has a history with government agencies and U.F.O. phenomena, kinda like the X-Files I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:06:36-08:00","id":1011238,"title":"","content":"Given how many of us have been working on fan made UFO splats, probably not best for deviant. But maybe Kansas City? Certainly an area with a torn up history and a fractured present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:15:14-08:00","id":1011240,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't know much regarding Deviant but Kansas City could work. What I do know seems to imply that we want a city where deviants end up more so than are created. Is that right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:20:37-08:00","id":1011241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1011222#post1011222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmm. Savannah for Beast, any hints for Deviant yet? Because maybe that could be Baltimore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free to crib from my write up as long as you PM me the draft first, I didn't fill out agendas for the individual compacts and conspiracies other than whether they support the 6-item agenda and I didn't include the Hunt Club in my write up. let me just put in a few suggestions for a few of the compacts and conspiracies:<br /> <br /> The local Hunt Club would follow the Melbourne rules as a means of humiliating VASCU by scaring off tourists and would mostly be linked to the old money plantation families as opposed to the new money young folks who make up the Abby in Savannah. Their membership includes a few heroes.<br /> <br /> VASCU would operate out of the FBI office in the north historic district. They probably investigated Ricky Jivens as a potential slasher and whether or not he was one, they would have stumbled on the Hunt Club presence in Savannah during that investigation and do their best to keep them from causing a panic with their rather theatrical murders of high profile targets.<br /> <br /> Network 0 plays a big role in the whole push the masquerade for tourist money plan. Their videos of Savannah's beasts have drawn in a lot of seekers of the weird, though commenters on the videos have accused them of being paid off by Savannah's tourism agencies, which isn't exactly wrong.<br /> <br /> The Education department compact (which I have yet to come up with a good name for) deals with a lot of beast students in the Jim Willaims schools, with the number of young begotten being 2nd only to the number of Sin-Eater students. They do their best to keep both the students and the public safe from each other, but every so (disturbingly) often, one of their truant officers becomes a Hero and has to be dealt with before they hurt a Beast student who decides to take a day off. Having the daughter of the Apex as one of those beast students presents it's own unique problems that require the compact to be very careful in parent teacher conferences with the Apex.<br /> <br /> The Georgia Historic Society Secert History Division collects stories about Georgia's most famous beasts and heroes, particulary the Apex and his extended bloodline as they search for the <b>Altamaha-ha </b>itself, hoping to gain it's extensive knowledge of Georgia's past.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T18:45:04-08:00","id":1011301,"title":"","content":"So would the Society not be an AKD front?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T06:36:05-08:00","id":1011480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1011301#post1011301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would the Society not be an AKD front?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.The society kicked the AKD and the loyalists out of Savannah after the two groups attempted to steal from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T09:45:52-08:00","id":1011538,"title":"","content":"Woah, how'd they do that to two major conspiracies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T09:49:21-08:00","id":1011540,"title":"","content":"If Memory serves the Loyalists of Thule are a compact, and their primarily researchers. Though I do wonder how they'd manage to kick out the militant Aegis Kai Doru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T13:07:48-08:00","id":1011625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=1011540#post1011540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Memory serves the Loyalists of Thule are a compact, and their primarily researchers. Though I do wonder how they'd manage to kick out the militant Aegis Kai Doru.</div> </div> </div> </div>Long Version:<br /> <br /> The historic society is backed by some very wealthy people, and politicians and corporations in Georgia IRL and the secret history division in the CofD includes some wealthy members as well, who are able to both supply their hunters with any equipment they need and create legal and finacial trouble for other compacts and conspiracies. Add in the fact that many of said wealthy members' children are members of the Ashwood Abby and the fact that the secret history division has the backing of TfV, and kicking out the AKD became much easier.<br /> <br /> Short version: the secret history division is sort of a combination of the Barret commission, the loyalists and the AKD, that includes both wealthy businessmen and politicians and scholars as members, and thus were able to attack the AKD and loyalists with both money and knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 12-03-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T13:35:18-08:00","id":1011640,"title":"","content":"So in other words, the Secret history division's well equipped hunters finished off those loyalists and AKD hunters that weren't taken down by the lawyers. They didn't so much defeat the AKD so much as they convinced them that Savannah wasn't worth dealing with the historic society, it's wealthy backers and their allies in other hunter groups and so the AKD left the city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T02:47:13-08:00","id":1011920,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that The Bear Lodge isn't really a city-focused group; so you would probably find larger number of them on the outskirts of many of the setting listed, or just out in the wilds of flyover country. That being said I'm sure lots of Vigilantes from the group would travel into the more dangerous cities for the sport and for duty","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Didn't anyone ever tell you not to bring claws to a gun fight?</span></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3786-leicsfox","name":"LeicsFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T02:50:02-08:00","id":1011922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/999231-the-vigil-in-the-us?p=999662#post999662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on a Princess city book for Detroit with Super_Dave and it includes a lot of hunters (you've got to have allies to interact with socally after all).<br /> <br /> Have a look if you're interested: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17vKlzHddpi-5PVLHy8yuonVH3rqbrawiNLDz35gBlGc/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...?pref=2&amp;pli=1#</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> this is cracking stuff; I really enjoyed reading through it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Didn't anyone ever tell you not to bring claws to a gun fight?</span></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3786-leicsfox","name":"LeicsFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T17:54:16-08:00","id":1012296,"title":"","content":"While I go back and forth with YMITC over Savannah, enjoy some Princess-Detroit<br /> <br /> <b>Detroit: A Hopeful Failure</b><br /> <br /> The Vigil in Detroit is dying, disastrously so. A war is underway between the magical beings known as &quot;princesses&quot;, the city's hunters, and the ancient enemies of the princesses. As Detroit falls to pieces under the dying American industrial sector, the compacts and conspiracies present in the city are scattered and disabled for one reason or another.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru: Invisible:</b> The AKD haven't been heard from since '03, when their headquarters was discovered abandoned and strewn with body parts, many could only imagine that they found something that no one wanted getting into the wider hunter community. With their relics destroyed and their files burned, the best guess anyone can make is that it has something to do with a recent discovery made by the AKD involving a lost site of the Odawa tribe.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones: Self-Loathing:</b> Civil war brews within the Cult of the Phoenix. While the Jagged Crescent continues to fill the conspiracy's coffers with the ill-gotten gains of drugs and crime, the Knife of Paradise is trying to pull the city back from the brink by providing basic social services like food kitchens and drives for babies clothes and diapers. With the Southern Temple trying to study the strange dark creatures and find their weaknesses, everyone on the outside that at least knows who the groups are sees civil war on the horizon.<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey: Reveling:</b> The sybarites are going wild in dying Detroit. Having moved safely out of the city years ago and ruling from their safe offices and high-rises during the day, the Abbey at least pays lip-service to groups like the Neighborhood Watch Alliance and CORD. But at night, the group loves to jump into the city and run wild through the abandoned neighborhoods and dying factories. They've obviously gotten on the wrong side of more than a few groups, but they could care less about the princesses and more about the ability to potentially capture and mount living darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>Barrett Commission: Panicked:</b> The Commission has come to accept that CORD is a problem, and that CORD also runs the city. Most of city hall is lost, so the Commission has instead set itself up in the power structure of Wayne County. Trying to figure out how to strike back in Detroit without exposing themselves, the Commission is beginning to fear that their focus on vampires has finally caught up with them in their inability to fight back in a meaningful way against the threat to Detroit.<br /> <br /> <b>Bear Lodge: Learning:</b> As a primarily rural group, the Lodge hunters in Detroit are primarily from the Vigilante motivation who have come to the city looking for targets they believe are worth their efforts. In this case, Detroit is a target-rich environment, and has become a kind of &quot;training ground&quot; for members wishing to learn more about how to handle hunting in an urban area. They've racked up an impressive stream of kills, but unfortunately for them the kills are things they have no idea about, or look disturbingly human.<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron Group: In a Candy Store:</b> The princesses and dark-creatures are new materials, and new materials are valuable to Cheiron's overall plan. The Group's Detroit subsidiary, Lake Shore Pharmaceutical Dynamics, is putting out dozens of cells a night recruited from the city's destitute, needy, and homeless. Casualties are easy to clean up too, since the bodies are sometimes absorbed into the creatures the agents are killed by.<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of St. George: Attacking:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Hunt Club: Nervous:</b> A few have attended one or two CORD meetings, and the sense they get from the group is that their place in the city's food chain is rapidly being endangered. At first operating off London Rules, the Club has since shifted to Melbourne out of what they claim is challenge, but what everyone else can tell is necessity. When you're one of the bigger kids on the block, someone comes to take a piece of you eventually. At least, that's how the Club sees it.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule: Involved:</b> Cultures around the world have legends involving darkness, as in nothing but a pure lack of anything. But no culture has ever said anything about darkness that <i>infects</i> the victims. Though the Loyalists have seen more than their fair share of horrors brought on by the human condition, records of creature like what are being found in Detroit have only been located in 35 places. Places that the Loyalists have sworn will never be again.<br /> <br /> <b>Long Night: Splintered: </b>Fractured between several various churches all trying to push Detroit towards a better future, the Long Night in the area are caught between the Hopeless going on nightly suicide runs and the Faithful who think that the downfall of Detroit is all the more proof that the end is just a new beginning. The Merciful have long ago boarded up their areas of the city, and instead focus on trying to heal those that are in most need. A number that climbs daily.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge: Guerrilla:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum: Resolute: </b>From their base in the St. Charles Borromeo parish complex, the Malleus stand as a stable force compared to the fractured Long Night. Offering community services that clothe and feed possibly thousands of Detroit residents, the Malleus have made sure to distance themselves from CORD after realizing that each policy the group enacted only led to an increase in the &quot;dark creatures&quot; hounding the city. They've also been the only group with a steady influx of new hunters willing to take up the candle with others, rather than striking out on their own.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero: Hunted: </b>NetZos in Detroit picked the wrong night to stage a break-in on a member of CORD. What was supposed to be a break-and-enter to steal some flash drives turned into a panicked flight and hurried upload to a secured server<b>. </b>Now all of Network Zero has access to what the cell found, but Network Zero's Detroit cells are in grave danger. CORD &quot;associates&quot; are willing to go through any lengths to achieve their masters' orders, and the most prominent has been, &quot;Find the information or else.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Night Watch: Rabid: </b>A broken city leads to broken minds, and the Detroit Watch are a prime example. The last straw was when the city outright started walling off neighborhoods to &quot;prevent crime&quot; from spreading. Realizing that they were being left to wither and die, the Watch struck back against every civic institution it could, but CORD has become their favorite target. While this has given the Watch vital intelligence on what CORD might truly be, their unwillingness to trust anyone has turned a possible intelligence coup into wasted information as the Watch continues to try and burn back the darkness, leading many who know <i>some</i> information about the princesses to fear they may become the perfect foundation for a cult of Stormwracked.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis: Hiding: </b>The scientists of ORAS are frightened, and no one can blame them. In 1983, a lab tried to contain a dark creature, and in 1984 the cell was buried with one member unaccounted for. Ever since the scientists have become the hunter, but to ORAS this means they might be close to something valuable. The dark creatures don't want people studying them it seems, but until the danger can pass Null Mysteriis members in Detroit have gone to the mattresses.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE: Torn Up: </b>For TFV, the game is running down. Worn, ragged, and desperate to try and find a new solution to old problems, TFV has been hemmed in to the Capitol Park district due to heavy casualties. Though Operation: AUTOMATIC HEARTLAND is under their aegis, several other teams and one MRU are also present in the city trying to gather intelligence on the &quot;darkness&quot; and to try and contact any princesses willing to possibly aid them in their fight. No offer is off the table, from amnesty to pardons to official government work.<br /> <br /> <b>Union: Fading: </b>UAWLocal911 is fighting a losing battle, and the Union in the greater Detroit area isn't doing so hot either. From cutbacks and downsizing during the day to constant skirmishes with darkness and monsters at night, the Union is becoming an increasingly outmoded group to many independent hunters. Though 911 is still leading the charge against the darkness and CORD, the group remains distant to the Princesses out of distrust after an incident involving some kinds of golems and several dead informants.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU: Noticing: </b>Despite the best efforts of the MIBs, VASCU isn't stupid enough to ignore when a problem is out there. Enough Wintergreen-capable agents have begun to realize exactly what stalks the city, and even without evidence are encouraging a greater Federal effort to look into CORD and groups sponsored by them. Of course, their more pressing concern are of several serial murders involving clay and missing body parts.<br /> <br /> <b>WIP</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 12-07-2016, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T22:22:55-08:00","id":1015984,"title":"","content":"Okay, I honestly have very little idea on how Beast actually works, please correct me where you all can.<br /> <br /> <b>Savannah: Something Wicked This Way Stays</b><br /> <br /> As the internet spread information through the Vigil at breakneck speed, stories began to spread and coalesce around Savannah. First, of a massive wave of terror brought on by one man, a gang leader known as &quot;Little Ricky&quot;. Second, that the police in the city were horribly corrupted and taking cash from anyone who could front it. Over time, the pieces were put together. First, that Ricky Jivens was a terror on par with the worst of the Prohibition Era gangsters that turned the city into his own personal shooting gallery, and that VASCU had to covertly assist in taking down. The second, that the city's long-serving chief of police Willie Lovett was so corrupt that his trial only just ended this past year. Of course, that's only the &quot;normal&quot; story. Under the surface, both men were heavily involved the the secret world that ran through Savannah, in this case the strange things that haunt the night and inspire terror in the lives of ordinary men. They just helped things along. What doesn't is how much the city is banking on the paranormal, hoping to draw in tourist dollars to the city by promoting the area as a haunted hotbed in the South. Many hunters are anxious, since the attention the city wants is exactly what many hunters don't need.<br /> <br /> <b>6th Sense Paranormal: Earning:</b> As the most well-known &quot;ghost hunters&quot; in the city, 6th Sense have crossed paths with the Vigil so often they're pretty much considering themselves a part of it, albeit a part that doesn't realize at all what it's getting into. They've only found ghosts and hauntings, meaning that if they ever found a vampire or werewolf, that the whole damn lid of secrecy might be blown off the second they bring in a tour group to see &quot;real&quot; monsters. They've already dangerously close with their tours involving the city's history of secret societies, more than most feel comfortable with.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones: Powerful:</b> With Jivens gone, the Jagged Crescent have propped up several other gang leaders in the city that could potentially take his place. The hope is that with these would-be kingpins under their control, the Cult of the Phoenix could control the Savannah underworld without losing innocent lives to the fighting between gangs. Of course, they've remained quiet on any connections they might have had with Little Ricky in the first place, or why his reign of terror lasted so long when he controlled never three-quarters of the city's drug market, drugs which they kept supplying.<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey: Schooling:</b> The Abbey in Savannah is a mixture of old Southern families and their young, rambunctious kids going to the Savannah College of Art and Design. While the older set watch and chuckle at the young children learning the ropes, the younger set of the Abbey are suddenly taking an interest in the strange creatures haunting the city. Just because their elders have never seen them doesn't mean they can't find them after all.<br /> <br /> <b>Barrett Commission: Flabbergasted:</b> Savannah should not have happened under their watch, but so focused on vampires, the Commission completely forgot about mundane corruption in the first place. Nevermind that they never expected it to come from <i>carnies</i> of all groups. With Jivens locked away and Chief Lovett finally out of the picture, the Commission is planning on trying to clean up the city, and centralize the corruption in <i>their</i> hands for a change.<br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero: Growing:</b> With their largest cell based out of SCAD, the Network is presently trying to carve out a niche in the city despite the entrenched presence of 6th Sense. Most people who find their way to Atlanta typically rely on 6th Sense to get their information, meaning that Network Zero has had to take a desperate step; going along with the Abbey on their hunts to film what happens.<br /> <br /> <b>Night Watch: Unsure:</b> With Jivens jailed in '91 and Lovett just recently out of power, the Night Watch desperately wants to start focusing on other problems. Unfortunately, the mass vampirization of the Maidens Blood Sisterhood in the city, coupled with the increased actions of the Abe, have forced the already bloodied Night Watch into questioning whether or not they shouldn't be in fact ramping up their actions in the city.<br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis: Unassuming:</b> ORAS keeps a quiet vigil in Atlanta, typically staying close to their ordinary lives and day jobs rather than going out for field research. The truth is that the scientists have been somewhat blinded by the stories being told about the monsters in Savannah, involving gorgons and dragons and such other mythic beasts. To the scientists, there's a suspension of disbelief, and then there's just plain making shit up, even in the Vigil.<br /> <br /> <b>WIP</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 12-14-2016, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T22:48:16-08:00","id":1015990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254<